WEBVTT

1
00:01:45.917 --> 00:01:50.500
O Goddess of Calcutta, hail!
May Your promises always prevail!

2
00:01:52.458 --> 00:01:55.125
May Your promises always prevail!

3
00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:59.333
- It's magic, isn't it, Sis?
- You doubt it?

4
00:02:01.458 --> 00:02:04.292
Ankur, listen. Don't stress.

5
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.625
Just tell me who did this.
I'll go easy on them.

6
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.000
Easy? You never go easy, Sis.

7
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:12.292
It's okay. It doesn't hurt too bad.

8
00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:14.333
Just tell me who did it.

9
00:02:14.542 --> 00:02:20.583
I'll make them pay
for every single scratch on you.

10
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.583
Manek Irani,

11
00:02:22.833 --> 00:02:24.042
Mahesh Anand,

12
00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.542
Ranjeet, Amrish, and Jeevan.

13
00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:30.250
Ask them to meet us behind the tank
tomorrow during lunch time.

14
00:02:30.333 --> 00:02:31.708
Leave the rest to me.

15
00:02:32.125 --> 00:02:33.875
Sis, I'm hungry.

16
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.500
I'll make you a sandwich right away.

17
00:02:37.042 --> 00:02:39.083
What's papa doing?

18
00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:40.958
I'm sorry, Satya.

19
00:02:41.458 --> 00:02:43.250
- Ankur, don't look!
- Papa…

20
00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.500
Satya.

21
00:03:20.208 --> 00:03:23.167
- Satya...
- There's a bouquet less in the gallery.

22
00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.208
The lamp oil under uncle's photo
is running out.

23
00:03:26.708 --> 00:03:30.458
- Satya...
- I found this in Uncle Sonu's room.

24
00:03:33.542 --> 00:03:36.083
Sorry, I'll flush it down the toilet.

25
00:03:37.625 --> 00:03:38.792
What were you saying?

26
00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:43.625
Kavita?

27
00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:56.667
Single malt for me.

28
00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.250
Yes, sir.

29
00:04:00.125 --> 00:04:03.250
Everyone says, "Mr. Mehtani
is running an orphanage."

30
00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:05.167
He offers distant relatives a home…

31
00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.458
…and helps arrange
their weddings as well…

32
00:04:07.542 --> 00:04:09.250
"…whereas they are just using you."

33
00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:12.125
But I don't believe that. I always say,

34
00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.750
it's God's bidding and I'm only the means.

35
00:04:15.708 --> 00:04:18.042
Right? Here's Satya!

36
00:04:18.125 --> 00:04:20.333
- The ceremony can't be delayed.
- It won't be.

37
00:04:20.417 --> 00:04:23.458
That's it! She's reassured us,
so there's nothing to worry.

38
00:04:23.542 --> 00:04:27.333
She is my cousin brother's daughter…

39
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:36.583
Satya…

40
00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.333
Satya, what are you doing?

41
00:04:41.208 --> 00:04:42.500
Who told you?

42
00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:46.208
Satya, I have to elope.
They won't accept Kavita.

43
00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:47.958
Let me go.

44
00:04:50.542 --> 00:04:51.792
Does uncle know?

45
00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.958
She's with my child. We have to elope.

46
00:05:04.083 --> 00:05:06.500
I want to marry Kavita,
not some rich girl.

47
00:05:07.708 --> 00:05:10.375
Out of all people,
you should understand that.

48
00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.833
Satya!

49
00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:20.792
Satya…

50
00:05:25.375 --> 00:05:28.542
Your future in-laws have dozens
of police cases against them.

51
00:05:28.625 --> 00:05:32.333
Listen. You two can run away today, okay?

52
00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:36.792
But her father will find you,
and he will kill her

53
00:05:36.917 --> 00:05:38.500
along with your child.

54
00:05:41.042 --> 00:05:42.333
Can you live with that?

55
00:05:44.208 --> 00:05:46.042
- Satya...
- Nakul.

56
00:05:47.708 --> 00:05:49.208
Do you love her?

57
00:05:50.958 --> 00:05:53.250
Then keep them alive.

58
00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:02.708
- What's going on, dear? All set?
- Yes.

59
00:06:03.458 --> 00:06:05.125
Why are you doing this?

60
00:06:05.208 --> 00:06:07.667
When will you change?
There's a wedding in the house.

61
00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:08.750
Yes.

62
00:06:09.083 --> 00:06:12.542
Hey, it's your big day today.
Get ready!

63
00:06:12.708 --> 00:06:14.167
- Yes.
- Come on!

64
00:06:20.833 --> 00:06:24.083
There's a job waiting for you in London,
and a school for your kid.

65
00:06:24.167 --> 00:06:28.333
Mr. Mehtani always looks after his staff.
Consider this your bonus.

66
00:06:28.417 --> 00:06:30.792
My love is not for sale, Satya!

67
00:06:31.042 --> 00:06:33.750
This money is not for you,
it's for your child.

68
00:06:34.083 --> 00:06:35.583
Where's Nakul?

69
00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.583
Nakul isn't coming.

70
00:06:43.083 --> 00:06:46.042
You love Nakul like your own son.

71
00:06:46.583 --> 00:06:49.042
You've organized
such a grand wedding for him…

72
00:06:49.333 --> 00:06:52.458
Stop whining!
Everything's solved. Go now!

73
00:06:52.875 --> 00:06:54.792
- Come on, cheer up.
- He did this…

74
00:06:54.875 --> 00:06:57.208
It's time to celebrate.
What's going on? Come on.

75
00:06:57.292 --> 00:07:00.542
Nakul's father-in-law insists
we don't miss the auspicious hour.

76
00:07:00.625 --> 00:07:02.500
- Come on.
- So don't be late.

77
00:07:06.042 --> 00:07:09.000
Satya, thank you very much.

78
00:07:09.833 --> 00:07:12.958
You know how short-tempered
these people are.

79
00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.625
And my work would also get stalled.

80
00:07:17.125 --> 00:07:21.708
Kavita needs to be taken care of
till her London visa comes through...

81
00:07:21.792 --> 00:07:25.167
I trust you. I'll cover all her expenses.

82
00:07:25.333 --> 00:07:27.125
- Okay.
- Listen.

83
00:07:27.625 --> 00:07:30.917
There's a wedding in the house,
and you're still in uniform? Go, change!

84
00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.375
Right away.

85
00:07:32.458 --> 00:07:35.500
Listen. Where's Ankur?

86
00:07:36.125 --> 00:07:38.917
I don't see him around.
He ought to be there.

87
00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:41.500
- Yes.
- We're family after all.

88
00:07:43.208 --> 00:07:44.208
Yes, Uncle.

89
00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.250
Have you seen Ankur?

90
00:07:59.667 --> 00:08:01.458
I sent his dinner to his room.

91
00:08:10.042 --> 00:08:11.250
Anku?

92
00:08:15.333 --> 00:08:17.333
I just greeted them and left.

93
00:08:20.417 --> 00:08:24.167
<i>Her gaze is lowered</i>

94
00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:29.500
<i>Are they full of longing?</i>

95
00:08:30.708 --> 00:08:33.917
<i>Her gaze is lowered…</i>

96
00:08:34.083 --> 00:08:35.792
Did your girlfriend dump you?

97
00:08:45.292 --> 00:08:46.667
Eat up.

98
00:08:47.875 --> 00:08:50.375
Stay hungry. Stay foolish.

99
00:08:53.167 --> 00:08:55.042
You'll always stay foolish.

100
00:08:55.292 --> 00:08:57.500
Listening to a sad ghazal at your age?

101
00:09:00.625 --> 00:09:02.917
Sis, the Alpha release is ready.

102
00:09:05.958 --> 00:09:07.417
Will uncle hear my pitch?

103
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.708
Of course.

104
00:09:19.083 --> 00:09:20.500
He's calling from an Indian number.

105
00:09:22.292 --> 00:09:23.417
Isn't he in Melbourne?

106
00:09:23.917 --> 00:09:26.277
He just wanted to skip the wedding,
else he'd be here today.

107
00:09:26.583 --> 00:09:27.792
Did he get expelled again?

108
00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:30.083
Sis, I can't answer for him.

109
00:09:31.125 --> 00:09:32.625
How am I responsible for that?

110
00:09:37.333 --> 00:09:38.583
But, Sis…

111
00:09:41.208 --> 00:09:43.375
- There's a get-together at his friend's...
- No.

112
00:09:56.542 --> 00:09:58.958
How long will you treat me like a kid?

113
00:09:59.792 --> 00:10:01.292
Kabir is my best friend.

114
00:10:01.375 --> 00:10:03.125
He is, and you know that.

115
00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:06.292
Why don't you go
and tell him not to talk to me?

116
00:10:08.292 --> 00:10:10.042
- Finish eating.
- Stay hungry!

117
00:10:21.208 --> 00:10:22.250
Hey, Jigre!

118
00:10:26.667 --> 00:10:27.667
Yes?

119
00:10:28.458 --> 00:10:30.958
If you want to go, then win and show!

120
00:10:31.958 --> 00:10:32.958
Let's go!

121
00:10:39.292 --> 00:10:41.208
Game to 11. Winner's ball.

122
00:10:41.292 --> 00:10:43.833
When did you play last? Can you remember?

123
00:10:44.333 --> 00:10:46.125
Inside 2, outside 3.

124
00:10:46.208 --> 00:10:47.750
No 3 pointers, Sis.

125
00:10:47.833 --> 00:10:48.833
Why?

126
00:10:49.958 --> 00:10:52.500
- Come on, put in some effort.
- Oh!

127
00:10:53.958 --> 00:10:55.042
You start!

128
00:10:55.708 --> 00:10:56.917
No check ball?

129
00:10:58.333 --> 00:10:59.458
No warm-up?

130
00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:02.292
Oh, I'm sorry.
You need a warm-up. I'll wait.

131
00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:56.542
What are you doing?

132
00:11:57.458 --> 00:11:58.292
Anku!

133
00:11:58.375 --> 00:11:59.417
Bye.

134
00:12:02.417 --> 00:12:03.542
So that's your game?

135
00:12:05.458 --> 00:12:06.458
Okay!

136
00:12:35.708 --> 00:12:36.917
Anku!

137
00:12:37.417 --> 00:12:39.750
I'm not going anywhere. Happy?

138
00:12:41.125 --> 00:12:43.208
Ankur, come on. I'm sorry.

139
00:12:44.083 --> 00:12:45.500
Okay, hold on.

140
00:12:45.875 --> 00:12:48.417
The game isn't over yet.
You can still win.

141
00:12:48.875 --> 00:12:50.000
Anku!

142
00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:17.875
The staff was saying
you don't want Kavita to be your boss

143
00:13:17.958 --> 00:13:21.083
and that's why
you are chasing her out of India.

144
00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.292
Who cares about what people say?

145
00:13:25.375 --> 00:13:28.917
The ones who care
jump off their balconies.

146
00:13:31.333 --> 00:13:33.875
Kavita will be fine in a few months.

147
00:13:34.375 --> 00:13:36.083
I'm worried about Kabir.

148
00:13:36.167 --> 00:13:38.583
Satya, no need to worry.

149
00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:41.625
Kabir thinks of you two as family.

150
00:13:42.167 --> 00:13:46.792
We are staff, Ratna,
and staff is always on duty.

151
00:13:49.875 --> 00:13:51.208
Double A!

152
00:13:55.375 --> 00:13:56.458
Rascal!

153
00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:02.542
Hey! What are you doing?

154
00:14:03.208 --> 00:14:05.625
- Get up.
- Come on, Kabir!

155
00:14:08.458 --> 00:14:10.601
We're meeting after six months,
and this is how you react!

156
00:14:10.625 --> 00:14:13.125
Give me a hug before giving the gifts.

157
00:14:13.208 --> 00:14:14.333
Come here!

158
00:14:16.833 --> 00:14:17.667
How are you, bro?

159
00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.167
Come here! How are you?

160
00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.917
- Fine. What about you?
- All good.

161
00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.833
Listen, get ready quickly.

162
00:14:23.917 --> 00:14:26.458
I've told my father
that you're giving him a presentation.

163
00:14:26.542 --> 00:14:28.792
I've exaggerated it greatly.
Please live up to it!

164
00:14:28.875 --> 00:14:30.375
- Okay.
- I'll see you downstairs.

165
00:14:32.208 --> 00:14:35.417
Trust me, Dad.
There's nothing like it in the market.

166
00:14:35.667 --> 00:14:37.333
He got rusticated again.

167
00:14:37.417 --> 00:14:38.667
Be quiet!

168
00:14:39.708 --> 00:14:41.917
- Mom, bless me.
- You're too much.

169
00:14:42.375 --> 00:14:44.042
- Not the hair, Mom.
- Well…

170
00:14:45.083 --> 00:14:47.417
Did you do the entire coding
and interface, Ankur?

171
00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.208
Yes. Yes, Uncle.

172
00:14:51.292 --> 00:14:52.292
Impressive!

173
00:14:52.708 --> 00:14:54.250
Just look at Ankur.

174
00:14:54.375 --> 00:14:57.875
He studied in an Indian school,
yet he's so smart. Whereas you…

175
00:14:57.958 --> 00:15:00.708
He is my brother after all.
He's your true heir.

176
00:15:02.875 --> 00:15:06.000
I'm adopted. I've always known it.

177
00:15:06.083 --> 00:15:08.500
Shut up! You talk nonsense.

178
00:15:09.792 --> 00:15:12.875
I know
Narayanan wants to invest in FinTech.

179
00:15:12.958 --> 00:15:15.875
So I'll speak to him, it'll be done.

180
00:15:16.833 --> 00:15:19.958
I knew you guys would work
wonders together.

181
00:15:20.083 --> 00:15:21.625
So it's actually happening?

182
00:15:21.708 --> 00:15:22.708
Yes, both of you!

183
00:15:23.917 --> 00:15:26.083
You rascal, why don't you ever react?

184
00:15:26.208 --> 00:15:29.208
Dude, get up! Come here. It's happening!

185
00:15:29.292 --> 00:15:31.708
Sis, come here.
It's so big! It's happening.

186
00:15:31.875 --> 00:15:34.458
I'm so happy!
Dad, it's happening, right?

187
00:15:34.667 --> 00:15:37.000
It won't happen
unless you go and start packing.

188
00:15:37.083 --> 00:15:39.309
You know what? Truer words
have not been said! Let's pack!

189
00:15:39.333 --> 00:15:42.167
- Satya, book them a charter flight.
- Okay.

190
00:15:42.833 --> 00:15:45.625
Uncle, thank you. Thank you so much.

191
00:15:46.458 --> 00:15:49.625
- Hey, come on. Well done!
- Thank you.

192
00:15:50.125 --> 00:15:52.917
Destination Hanshi Dao.

193
00:15:55.708 --> 00:15:58.167
Text me when you take off and land.
Eat on time!

194
00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:02.167
Just focus on your work.
Don't go anywhere unnecessarily.

195
00:16:02.458 --> 00:16:03.458
Okay?

196
00:16:04.167 --> 00:16:07.500
Am I allowed to breathe? To live a little?

197
00:16:07.958 --> 00:16:09.542
Oh, God, Sis!

198
00:16:09.833 --> 00:16:13.542
Don't worry. I'm with him. Let's go.

199
00:16:13.792 --> 00:16:15.875
- Hey, stop!
- What happened?

200
00:16:16.125 --> 00:16:19.250
- Mom, please.
- Of course, she must bless you.

201
00:16:20.458 --> 00:16:22.292
See you. Come on.

202
00:16:37.667 --> 00:16:39.458
Stop crying!

203
00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:43.250
- They'll be all right.
- Yes.

204
00:16:49.458 --> 00:16:53.667
How quickly they've grown.
Now they're off on a business trip.

205
00:17:09.958 --> 00:17:11.458
<i>I wanna love you</i>

206
00:17:11.667 --> 00:17:13.208
<i>I wanna uhh you</i>

207
00:17:13.292 --> 00:17:16.500
<i>Good luck follows me wherever I go</i>

208
00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:20.625
<i>I wanna tell you something in Telugu</i>

209
00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.292
<i>You smell better than Biryani</i>

210
00:17:23.708 --> 00:17:27.833
<i>'Cos I'm a Pan India Area King</i>

211
00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:31.083
<i>Pan India Area King</i>

212
00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:35.167
<i>+91 Ring-ring-ring</i>

213
00:17:35.917 --> 00:17:38.750
<i>Pan India Area King</i>

214
00:17:52.125 --> 00:17:53.875
<i>Can you do it with music, bro?</i>

215
00:17:54.208 --> 00:17:57.250
<i>Sweet Juliet, hip Majnu</i>

216
00:17:57.875 --> 00:18:01.042
<i>I'm richer than the richest</i>

217
00:18:01.625 --> 00:18:02.917
<i>When I call you</i>

218
00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:05.125
<i>Let's dip ourselves in sugar</i>

219
00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:08.000
<i>We'll add milk and make Payasam to relish</i>

220
00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:11.958
<i>'Cos I'm a Pan India Area King</i>

221
00:18:12.875 --> 00:18:15.333
<i>Pan India Area King</i>

222
00:18:16.542 --> 00:18:19.417
<i>+91 Ring-ring-ring</i>

223
00:18:20.208 --> 00:18:23.208
<i>Pan India Area King</i>

224
00:18:24.458 --> 00:18:28.542
<i>Oh, you called? I asked you to call?</i>

225
00:18:28.958 --> 00:18:30.583
<i>I regret to inform you</i>

226
00:18:30.875 --> 00:18:34.208
<i>But Pan India Area King
Is too busy for love</i>

227
00:18:34.917 --> 00:18:37.958
<i>I don't have a fortress,
But I'm still the king</i>

228
00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:41.375
<i>Pan India Area King</i>

229
00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:45.625
<i>Pan India Area King</i>

230
00:18:46.083 --> 00:18:48.958
<i>+91 Ring-ring-ring</i>

231
00:18:49.083 --> 00:18:51.833
- Oh, no! Kabir, slow down.
- Let me think.

232
00:18:51.917 --> 00:18:54.208
- Just let me think.
- Hold on.

233
00:18:54.542 --> 00:18:57.083
- We should've hired a taxi.
- I'll handle it.

234
00:19:00.292 --> 00:19:01.434
What's the penalty for drunk driving?

235
00:19:01.458 --> 00:19:03.917
- Hope we don't get thrown into jail.
- Hold on.

236
00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:05.458
It'll be fine.

237
00:19:07.208 --> 00:19:09.292
I'm sorry, sir. Is there any problem?

238
00:19:09.375 --> 00:19:11.917
Sir, we were just headed to the hotel.

239
00:19:14.458 --> 00:19:16.708
- There's nothing in the car, sir…
- Get out!

240
00:19:16.792 --> 00:19:19.792
- Get out!
- Sir, we were just…

241
00:19:20.375 --> 00:19:22.542
Sir…

242
00:19:23.958 --> 00:19:26.167
Sir, that's my passport. I'm from India.

243
00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.542
We're just going to the hotel.
That's all, sir.

244
00:19:51.208 --> 00:19:53.625
- Please, I need to talk to my dad...
- Get inside!

245
00:19:53.708 --> 00:19:55.417
Ankur, don't say a word.

246
00:19:56.708 --> 00:19:58.250
Come on.

247
00:20:08.083 --> 00:20:10.125
Mr. Mehtani, I understand
what you're saying

248
00:20:10.208 --> 00:20:13.542
but Hanshi Dao shows no mercy
to drug offenders. It's death.

249
00:20:13.625 --> 00:20:17.208
<i>- I can try to save one of them.</i>
- Yes.

250
00:20:18.958 --> 00:20:20.417
Yes, I know.

251
00:20:21.792 --> 00:20:22.792
Do your best.

252
00:20:29.708 --> 00:20:31.167
What is it?

253
00:20:31.583 --> 00:20:34.250
I can't get through to Kabir.

254
00:20:34.792 --> 00:20:37.167
There should be a way. Just find out.

255
00:20:37.417 --> 00:20:39.042
Talk to Narayanan.

256
00:20:39.167 --> 00:20:40.375
Hello?

257
00:20:41.125 --> 00:20:42.250
Yes?

258
00:20:42.625 --> 00:20:45.958
- Yes. Satyabhama Anand.
- I'll talk to you later.

259
00:20:46.292 --> 00:20:47.500
Yes, please.

260
00:20:49.333 --> 00:20:50.500
Sis?

261
00:20:50.583 --> 00:20:53.042
Ankur, did you screw up?

262
00:20:53.375 --> 00:20:55.333
Did you do drugs?

263
00:20:55.417 --> 00:20:57.500
- No, I didn't.
- Okay.

264
00:20:57.625 --> 00:21:00.458
Did anyone use your phone?
Did Kabir use it? No?

265
00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:02.875
Are you sure your blood sample is clean?

266
00:21:02.958 --> 00:21:04.792
Don't worry, you'll be okay…

267
00:21:04.875 --> 00:21:05.958
Blood sample?

268
00:21:06.042 --> 00:21:08.250
Ankur, how is Kabir?

269
00:21:08.667 --> 00:21:11.708
Why can't I talk to him?
What have you guys done?

270
00:21:11.792 --> 00:21:15.500
You were supposed to look after him.
How could you let this happen?

271
00:21:15.583 --> 00:21:17.917
Give it to me. Stop this drama!

272
00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:21.333
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Uncle, I have no idea what's happening.

273
00:21:21.417 --> 00:21:23.958
- I warned Kabir.
- <i>Relax. You'll be fine.</i>

274
00:21:24.708 --> 00:21:26.958
I'll fix it, Ankur.

275
00:21:27.292 --> 00:21:29.917
Lawyer Jaswant is on his way.

276
00:21:30.125 --> 00:21:33.708
He'll take care of everything.
Just do as he says, okay?

277
00:21:37.542 --> 00:21:39.708
- You want to go home?
- Of course!

278
00:21:40.208 --> 00:21:42.250
Then do precisely as I say.

279
00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:45.667
Follow my instructions and say
exactly what I'm telling you to say.

280
00:21:52.667 --> 00:21:55.458
<i>Two officers will come in once I leave.</i>

281
00:21:56.042 --> 00:21:58.542
<i>You're going to tell them
those drugs don't belong to you</i>

282
00:21:59.167 --> 00:22:00.500
<i>but to Ankur.</i>

283
00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:04.750
<i>That he panicked
and stuffed them in your pocket.</i>

284
00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:07.250
- What?
- That's what you're going to tell them.

285
00:22:07.333 --> 00:22:08.875
Exactly these words.

286
00:22:09.792 --> 00:22:12.375
Ankur knows absolutely nothing about this.

287
00:22:12.958 --> 00:22:15.083
It's all my fault.
He doesn't know anything about it.

288
00:22:15.167 --> 00:22:17.167
We have no other option, dear.

289
00:22:19.458 --> 00:22:23.083
Uncle, I don't know what you think,
but he's like my brother.

290
00:22:23.292 --> 00:22:24.625
I can't do that to him.

291
00:22:28.417 --> 00:22:30.250
It's okay, come.

292
00:22:34.458 --> 00:22:39.042
They show no mercy to drug offenders
in this country. It's death.

293
00:22:39.125 --> 00:22:41.833
I can't die here! Get me out, please.

294
00:22:42.083 --> 00:22:46.583
Just help me. Get me out of here.
I don't want to stay here. Please.

295
00:22:47.625 --> 00:22:49.083
Hello.

296
00:22:50.875 --> 00:22:51.875
How are you?

297
00:22:53.958 --> 00:22:56.250
Recognize me? I'm Jaswant.

298
00:22:56.875 --> 00:22:59.083
Mr. Mehtani must've told you about me.
I'm also family.

299
00:22:59.167 --> 00:23:01.542
The things you kids do!

300
00:23:02.375 --> 00:23:03.375
We have a little problem.

301
00:23:05.125 --> 00:23:08.208
You know that Kabir
has two drug related cases in India.

302
00:23:08.292 --> 00:23:10.917
A third case is very bad for him.

303
00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:13.667
He could face the death penalty.

304
00:23:14.958 --> 00:23:15.958
So don't worry.

305
00:23:16.208 --> 00:23:17.375
When the cops come here,

306
00:23:17.458 --> 00:23:21.167
tell them that the drugs
don't belong to Kabir, but to you.

307
00:23:23.292 --> 00:23:25.125
Sir, what are you saying?

308
00:23:26.125 --> 00:23:29.750
<i>See, we'll prove
that there was less than one gram.</i>

309
00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.125
<i>You'll be back home in a few months.</i>

310
00:23:33.208 --> 00:23:35.083
<i>And the Mehtani family
will be there for you.</i>

311
00:23:35.167 --> 00:23:36.458
Sir, what about my career?

312
00:23:37.042 --> 00:23:39.208
What happens to my career
if I'm convicted?

313
00:23:39.292 --> 00:23:43.125
We're talking about Kabir's life,
and you're worried about your career?

314
00:23:43.208 --> 00:23:44.292
Sir.

315
00:23:46.042 --> 00:23:48.958
<i>This is the only option
if Kabir has to live.</i>

316
00:23:55.625 --> 00:23:57.000
Sir, I want talk to Kabir.

317
00:23:57.083 --> 00:23:59.083
- Impossible.
- Sir, I must talk to Kabir.

318
00:23:59.167 --> 00:24:01.583
It's impossible, I'm telling you.

319
00:24:02.667 --> 00:24:03.500
Okay?

320
00:24:03.583 --> 00:24:07.875
I know that he
and the whole Mehtani family

321
00:24:08.542 --> 00:24:10.542
are depending on you.

322
00:24:11.292 --> 00:24:14.583
Your career is absolutely safe
with the Mehtani family.

323
00:24:14.875 --> 00:24:16.875
You are a part of them.

324
00:24:17.708 --> 00:24:18.958
That's why I'm here.

325
00:24:21.708 --> 00:24:23.583
Your brother needs your help, dear.

326
00:24:43.667 --> 00:24:48.208
For official records,
you just need to say, "Yes, I agree".

327
00:24:51.708 --> 00:24:54.208
Admit you're a drug trafficker.

328
00:24:54.333 --> 00:24:55.667
Hey! Look at me!

329
00:24:56.583 --> 00:24:58.083
Admit you're a drug trafficker

330
00:24:58.167 --> 00:25:01.750
and you got these drugs
to sell in the market.

331
00:25:02.292 --> 00:25:05.667
Okay? Now you can say 'yes' or 'no'.

332
00:25:08.042 --> 00:25:09.167
Yes.

333
00:25:10.292 --> 00:25:11.708
Yes, I agree.

334
00:25:13.875 --> 00:25:14.875
Where is Kabir?

335
00:25:15.083 --> 00:25:16.083
<i>Kabir is fine</i>

336
00:25:16.375 --> 00:25:19.292
<i>but I'm sorry about Ankur.
There was no other way.</i>

337
00:25:19.375 --> 00:25:20.375
Okay.

338
00:25:25.125 --> 00:25:28.333
The State Vs. Ankur Anand.

339
00:25:29.375 --> 00:25:33.958
Do you agree to this confession?

340
00:25:35.042 --> 00:25:36.917
This confession in front of me,

341
00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:40.042
do you agree saying 'yes' to it,
Mr. Anand?

342
00:25:41.958 --> 00:25:42.958
Yes.

343
00:25:44.458 --> 00:25:49.125
Death by electrocution in three months.

344
00:25:51.792 --> 00:25:55.417
Death by electrocution in three months.

345
00:25:56.792 --> 00:25:59.333
What did he say!

346
00:26:00.625 --> 00:26:02.542
This has to be a mistake! It's not me!

347
00:26:03.833 --> 00:26:05.458
It's a mistake!

348
00:26:07.083 --> 00:26:09.083
Mr. Mehtani has sent you
some local currency.

349
00:26:09.708 --> 00:26:10.708
Is this charity?

350
00:26:11.208 --> 00:26:14.667
I'll have many expenses there.
I can't keep asking him.

351
00:26:14.750 --> 00:26:17.684
Ask him to transfer Rs. 2 crore and
arrange a charter flight to Hanshi Dao.

352
00:26:17.708 --> 00:26:19.167
- What?
- You heard me.

353
00:26:28.500 --> 00:26:30.667
- Sis, I'm really sorry.
- Kabir.

354
00:26:30.792 --> 00:26:33.458
I didn't mean for it to happen.
I'm really sorry.

355
00:26:33.542 --> 00:26:36.333
Kabir, let's go. Go, sit in the car.

356
00:26:37.375 --> 00:26:41.333
I'm really sorry. We tried everything.

357
00:26:49.375 --> 00:26:50.208
Yeah?

358
00:26:50.292 --> 00:26:52.542
<i>A fire has broken out
in Mr. Mehtani's office!</i>

359
00:26:52.625 --> 00:26:53.625
What?

360
00:26:54.708 --> 00:26:55.708
A fire?

361
00:27:14.208 --> 00:27:15.625
<i>What's papa doing?</i>

362
00:27:15.708 --> 00:27:17.125
<i>Ankur, don't look!</i>

363
00:27:17.333 --> 00:27:18.625
<i>I'm sorry, Satya.</i>

364
00:27:19.375 --> 00:27:21.208
<i>Just tell me who did it.</i>

365
00:27:21.417 --> 00:27:25.333
<i>I'll make them pay
for every single scratch on you.</i>

366
00:27:28.167 --> 00:27:29.542
Could I get you something?

367
00:27:31.625 --> 00:27:32.833
Everything.

368
00:27:33.458 --> 00:27:35.292
May I get you the menu?

369
00:27:36.250 --> 00:27:37.667
Give me everything.

370
00:27:46.125 --> 00:27:48.833
<i>Jiang Ge prison
is situated on Ying Zhu island.</i>

371
00:27:48.958 --> 00:27:52.583
<i>Ying Zhu island has been
a part of Hanshi Dao since 2014.</i>

372
00:27:53.083 --> 00:27:55.583
<i>Our jail is fully automated.</i>

373
00:27:55.667 --> 00:28:00.208
<i>We were the first in Hanshi Dao
to be part of the digital universe.</i>

374
00:28:00.917 --> 00:28:06.417
<i>Prisoners wear color coded t-shirts
according to their crime.</i>

375
00:28:06.625 --> 00:28:11.833
<i>Agitators of separatist movements
are held in different cells.</i>

376
00:28:12.250 --> 00:28:16.292
<i>Long live the revolution, Geming Wansui,
Hanshi Dao Down Down!</i>

377
00:28:16.417 --> 00:28:19.167
<i>These slogans are banned.</i>

378
00:28:20.083 --> 00:28:22.708
Prison rules and guidelines.

379
00:28:23.750 --> 00:28:28.125
This is the only holy book
you need to think about.

380
00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:31.542
The rules of conduct
that will apply to you

381
00:28:31.667 --> 00:28:34.875
will also apply to me and my officers.

382
00:28:35.333 --> 00:28:36.875
You must understand.

383
00:28:36.958 --> 00:28:40.292
You and I, we are in the same boat.

384
00:28:40.375 --> 00:28:44.250
We have been at the forefront
for technology and innovation.

385
00:28:44.458 --> 00:28:46.375
But at the core of it…

386
00:28:46.500 --> 00:28:48.643
- Sir, could you please change your gloves?
- Come here.

387
00:28:48.667 --> 00:28:50.268
Sir, could you please change
your gloves first?

388
00:28:50.292 --> 00:28:52.542
You haven't changed your gloves, sir.

389
00:28:52.625 --> 00:28:53.792
- Sir!
- Hey!

390
00:28:58.500 --> 00:28:59.875
- Hey!
- Yes, sir?

391
00:29:01.125 --> 00:29:03.542
- Go, wait in my office. Now.
- Okay.

392
00:29:04.667 --> 00:29:06.747
- Sir, he didn't change his gloves.
- You keep quiet!

393
00:29:08.667 --> 00:29:10.417
Send in another officer.

394
00:29:12.250 --> 00:29:13.750
Sir, are you Indian?

395
00:29:13.833 --> 00:29:15.750
- Stay behind!
- Sir, are you Indian?

396
00:29:16.333 --> 00:29:17.333
Stay behind!

397
00:29:17.375 --> 00:29:19.375
- Sir, do you understand Hindi?
- Stand behind!

398
00:29:19.458 --> 00:29:22.125
- Sir, I'm innocent. I was framed.
- Stand behind!

399
00:29:22.208 --> 00:29:25.417
- I'm innocent. I was forced to confess.
- He is not even listening to me.

400
00:29:25.500 --> 00:29:28.458
They said I'd get three months,
not the death sentence.

401
00:29:29.250 --> 00:29:32.292
Sir, I'm innocent. I'm an engineer.
Why would I do all this?

402
00:29:32.375 --> 00:29:34.750
If my great-grandfather was alive,

403
00:29:34.875 --> 00:29:37.083
then maybe he could understand
what you're saying.

404
00:29:37.167 --> 00:29:39.875
I do not, because I am not Indian.
You understand or not?

405
00:29:39.958 --> 00:29:42.958
Yes, sir. My name is Ankur Anand.

406
00:29:43.042 --> 00:29:45.458
Sir, I'm an orphan. I only have my sister.

407
00:29:46.333 --> 00:29:48.333
Sir, I didn't do anything wrong…

408
00:29:48.542 --> 00:29:52.833
Boy, you must learn to listen.
You understand or not?

409
00:29:52.958 --> 00:29:54.708
I listened to you just now, right?

410
00:29:54.792 --> 00:29:56.583
Now you must listen! Stand straight.

411
00:29:56.667 --> 00:29:59.000
Put your hands down. Stand straight.

412
00:29:59.583 --> 00:30:00.583
Put your hands apart.

413
00:30:02.500 --> 00:30:08.167
Yes, lift up your tongue. Up. Down. Good.

414
00:30:10.042 --> 00:30:11.750
It's okay.

415
00:30:13.500 --> 00:30:14.500
Clear!

416
00:30:15.375 --> 00:30:18.583
Bend over. Spread your legs.

417
00:30:19.500 --> 00:30:20.500
Cough!

418
00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:22.167
Cough!

419
00:30:23.542 --> 00:30:24.708
Clear!

420
00:30:24.792 --> 00:30:27.333
Okay, clean. Up! Come here.

421
00:30:27.417 --> 00:30:29.042
Make sure you put on fresh gloves.

422
00:30:30.250 --> 00:30:31.250
Come.

423
00:30:42.542 --> 00:30:44.125
You are purple shirt?

424
00:30:44.875 --> 00:30:46.435
You don't have a lot of time, you know.

425
00:30:47.500 --> 00:30:50.750
Read this, cover to cover. Understand?

426
00:30:50.958 --> 00:30:52.625
Turn to your right. Carry on.

427
00:30:52.708 --> 00:30:54.792
Next! Come forward.

428
00:31:09.958 --> 00:31:11.792
<i>They call this a city.</i>

429
00:31:12.833 --> 00:31:14.583
<i>That's what they say.</i>

430
00:31:15.833 --> 00:31:19.875
<i>But the law of the jungle rules here.
The jungle.</i>

431
00:31:21.250 --> 00:31:23.667
<i>The lizard eats the ant.</i>

432
00:31:24.583 --> 00:31:26.917
<i>The frog eats the lizard.</i>

433
00:31:27.417 --> 00:31:29.917
<i>The snake swallows the frog.</i>

434
00:31:31.667 --> 00:31:34.125
<i>The mongoose gulps down the snake.</i>

435
00:31:36.208 --> 00:31:38.583
<i>The wolf sucks the blood of the mongoose.</i>

436
00:31:39.250 --> 00:31:41.458
<i>The tiger devours the wolf.</i>

437
00:31:41.667 --> 00:31:44.458
<i>Here, the strong survive</i>

438
00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:48.500
<i>by killing the weak. Get it? They kill.</i>

439
00:32:38.167 --> 00:32:39.542
Body check.

440
00:32:46.792 --> 00:32:49.250
Stop! Store your luggage in the locker.

441
00:32:49.917 --> 00:32:51.375
M-My brother…

442
00:32:52.958 --> 00:32:54.542
Store your luggage in the locker.

443
00:32:55.083 --> 00:32:57.208
Sorry, the locker…

444
00:32:59.958 --> 00:33:01.042
Keep the bags.

445
00:33:02.708 --> 00:33:04.125
- Phone.
- Phone also.

446
00:33:04.208 --> 00:33:05.583
- Here.
- 50 Shin.

447
00:33:08.917 --> 00:33:10.333
- Here.
- Token.

448
00:33:10.708 --> 00:33:11.708
Thank you.

449
00:33:15.500 --> 00:33:19.000
Do not run! Stop. Go over here.

450
00:33:19.167 --> 00:33:20.167
Where to go?

451
00:33:22.583 --> 00:33:23.583
Where to go?

452
00:33:24.542 --> 00:33:25.708
Visiting my brother.

453
00:33:26.750 --> 00:33:27.750
There?

454
00:33:32.167 --> 00:33:33.167
Excuse me.

455
00:33:34.083 --> 00:33:34.917
Yes?

456
00:33:35.042 --> 00:33:37.042
- Am I late?
- Hold on!

457
00:33:37.167 --> 00:33:39.917
- Am I late, sir?
- Hold on. I'm giving you a pass.

458
00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:43.250
My brother… Ankur Anand
is my brother's name.

459
00:33:46.167 --> 00:33:47.250
Okay.

460
00:33:48.833 --> 00:33:50.167
Where to go?

461
00:33:50.292 --> 00:33:52.250
Calm down.

462
00:33:52.875 --> 00:33:54.500
- You're not late.
- Okay.

463
00:33:54.750 --> 00:33:57.500
Please sit. I'll call. Please sit.

464
00:34:20.292 --> 00:34:23.083
Satyabhama?

465
00:34:25.375 --> 00:34:27.625
This is the only face-to-face visit
you have.

466
00:34:27.708 --> 00:34:31.625
After this, make application
for tele-visit. You follow?

467
00:34:37.542 --> 00:34:38.917
- How do I look?
- What?

468
00:34:41.458 --> 00:34:42.458
Do I look sad?

469
00:34:44.208 --> 00:34:46.208
Oh, yeah. Little sad.

470
00:34:53.917 --> 00:34:55.167
Now?

471
00:34:55.708 --> 00:34:56.708
Very sad.

472
00:35:03.042 --> 00:35:04.542
That way.

473
00:35:16.958 --> 00:35:20.375
<i>Even if the stars disappear
Or the moon hides</i>

474
00:35:20.583 --> 00:35:22.833
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

475
00:35:25.625 --> 00:35:29.167
<i>Whether something happens or not</i>

476
00:35:29.292 --> 00:35:31.583
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

477
00:35:34.458 --> 00:35:37.958
<i>If a terrible storm encircles you</i>

478
00:35:38.042 --> 00:35:40.792
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

479
00:35:43.208 --> 00:35:46.625
<i>Even if the stars disappear
Or the moon hides</i>

480
00:35:46.750 --> 00:35:48.917
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

481
00:35:51.625 --> 00:35:59.625
<i>Where has this path led me?</i>

482
00:36:00.417 --> 00:36:08.083
<i>You'll follow me wherever I go</i>

483
00:36:08.917 --> 00:36:16.917
<i>Where has this path led me?</i>

484
00:36:17.875 --> 00:36:24.833
<i>You'll follow me wherever I go</i>

485
00:36:26.708 --> 00:36:30.042
<i>If the world turns its back on you</i>

486
00:36:30.375 --> 00:36:32.708
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

487
00:36:35.292 --> 00:36:38.792
<i>If the dark clouds hide the glorious sun</i>

488
00:36:39.500 --> 00:36:41.917
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

489
00:36:44.333 --> 00:36:47.708
<i>If the sea dries up and the sky falls</i>

490
00:36:47.792 --> 00:36:49.375
<i>I'll keep you close…</i>

491
00:36:49.542 --> 00:36:51.125
Ankur.

492
00:36:51.708 --> 00:36:53.958
They tell me
I have only three months to live.

493
00:36:58.458 --> 00:37:00.083
Listen to me.

494
00:37:01.833 --> 00:37:04.625
Ankur.

495
00:37:08.750 --> 00:37:10.375
Look! Look at me!

496
00:37:12.833 --> 00:37:14.667
You are my brother, aren't you?

497
00:37:16.667 --> 00:37:19.125
So I'll always protect you.

498
00:37:20.625 --> 00:37:24.083
I will not let any harm come to you.

499
00:37:25.917 --> 00:37:27.083
Ever.

500
00:37:27.667 --> 00:37:34.625
<i>Where has this path led me?</i>

501
00:37:36.375 --> 00:37:43.750
<i>You'll follow me wherever I go</i>

502
00:37:45.125 --> 00:37:52.667
<i>Where has this path led me?</i>

503
00:37:53.875 --> 00:38:01.458
<i>You'll follow me wherever I am</i>

504
00:38:02.833 --> 00:38:06.083
<i>If the world turns its back on you</i>

505
00:38:06.375 --> 00:38:08.792
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

506
00:38:11.583 --> 00:38:14.833
<i>If the dark clouds hide the glorious sun</i>

507
00:38:15.042 --> 00:38:17.292
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

508
00:38:20.500 --> 00:38:23.667
<i>If the sea dries up and the sky falls</i>

509
00:38:23.792 --> 00:38:26.417
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

510
00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:32.333
<i>Even if the stars disappear
Or the moon hides</i>

511
00:38:32.625 --> 00:38:34.625
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

512
00:38:37.500 --> 00:38:44.875
<i>Where has this path led me?</i>

513
00:38:46.167 --> 00:38:53.500
<i>You'll follow me wherever I go</i>

514
00:38:54.833 --> 00:39:02.333
<i>Where has this path led me?</i>

515
00:39:03.458 --> 00:39:11.000
<i>You'll follow me wherever I go</i>

516
00:39:18.875 --> 00:39:22.333
<i>All new inmates of Cell Block B4.</i>

517
00:39:22.542 --> 00:39:26.375
<i>This is OIC Landa. Welcome.</i>

518
00:39:27.750 --> 00:39:30.333
<i>You all have been given
access to counseling</i>

519
00:39:30.458 --> 00:39:34.875
<i>to help you adjust mentally
to your new conditions</i>

520
00:39:35.167 --> 00:39:39.000
<i>which in turn will be good
for your rehabilitation.</i>

521
00:39:39.583 --> 00:39:40.833
<i>But before that</i>

522
00:39:41.417 --> 00:39:44.417
<i>all of you in purple t-shirts on death row</i>

523
00:39:44.667 --> 00:39:48.292
<i>especially those amongst you
on drug charges,</i>

524
00:39:48.958 --> 00:39:51.292
<i>let me make some things clear.</i>

525
00:39:52.333 --> 00:39:56.542
<i>Listen to this, gentlemen,
and listen very carefully,</i>

526
00:39:57.500 --> 00:39:59.917
<i>for it will help ease your pain,</i>

527
00:40:00.667 --> 00:40:02.292
<i>clear your confusion</i>

528
00:40:02.583 --> 00:40:04.958
<i>and it'll put your hope to rest.</i>

529
00:40:05.833 --> 00:40:08.000
<i>Your fathers, your mothers,</i>

530
00:40:08.125 --> 00:40:12.250
<i>your brothers, uncles, sisters…
Got friends? Got cousins?</i>

531
00:40:12.833 --> 00:40:16.833
<i>All of them outside
will be trying to delay the inevitable…</i>

532
00:40:17.667 --> 00:40:18.833
<i>your death.</i>

533
00:40:20.125 --> 00:40:21.958
But it's a waste of time.

534
00:40:23.208 --> 00:40:25.292
It's a waste of time.

535
00:40:25.375 --> 00:40:29.292
When it comes to immigrants here,
they make examples out of them.

536
00:40:33.042 --> 00:40:37.083
Coco! Why didn't you fill the generator
with diesel?

537
00:40:37.167 --> 00:40:39.917
What am I paying you for?
To dry your nails?

538
00:40:40.250 --> 00:40:41.750
- Sir, Satya.
- Yes?

539
00:40:42.375 --> 00:40:45.417
Ankur Anand, my brother.
We had an appointment today at 4 p.m.

540
00:40:45.500 --> 00:40:48.542
- Right, right. Ankur. Narcotics, yes?
- Yes.

541
00:40:48.625 --> 00:40:53.292
You see, his sentence
is such that time is ticking for him.

542
00:40:54.333 --> 00:40:58.167
The clock hands are moving.
I can slow them down a bit.

543
00:40:58.667 --> 00:40:59.917
That is all I can do.

544
00:41:00.083 --> 00:41:03.542
Sir, I… I want to take him home.

545
00:41:04.250 --> 00:41:07.750
<i>This isn't like an Indian jail.</i>

546
00:41:08.583 --> 00:41:10.292
<i>It's clean, the food is good.</i>

547
00:41:10.375 --> 00:41:12.167
<i>Recreation is good.</i>

548
00:41:12.750 --> 00:41:15.083
<i>You think he chose to be in jail?</i>

549
00:41:15.667 --> 00:41:17.268
If it was someone you loved,
would you say,

550
00:41:17.292 --> 00:41:19.625
"Eat, drink and be merry?"

551
00:41:20.208 --> 00:41:22.833
In this case? That's what I'd say.

552
00:41:23.417 --> 00:41:25.250
<i>I would immediately appeal</i>

553
00:41:25.375 --> 00:41:29.375
<i>then try and get the sentence delayed
for a few months.</i>

554
00:41:31.542 --> 00:41:34.333
<i>Our NGOs are here to help Indians</i>

555
00:41:34.583 --> 00:41:38.583
<i>but please don't distribute your posters.
The government will object.</i>

556
00:41:38.667 --> 00:41:41.125
Especially since it's a case of narcotics.

557
00:41:41.208 --> 00:41:42.917
Then we won't be able to help at all.

558
00:41:44.500 --> 00:41:47.500
<i>The presidential pardon
is only possible in two instances.</i>

559
00:41:47.583 --> 00:41:51.125
<i>If the convict is underage,
or mentally unstable.</i>

560
00:41:54.792 --> 00:41:57.625
Hey! Pass the ball!

561
00:42:01.083 --> 00:42:02.750
Brother, pass the ball!

562
00:42:03.250 --> 00:42:04.250
Is he deaf?

563
00:42:04.875 --> 00:42:09.792
- Rayyan.
- Rayyan! Let's go.

564
00:42:10.333 --> 00:42:12.167
- Crazy guy!
- Ready to lose again?

565
00:42:12.250 --> 00:42:14.500
- Hey!
- I've seen your face before.

566
00:42:16.958 --> 00:42:18.250
New boy!

567
00:42:21.792 --> 00:42:22.917
Hello.

568
00:42:28.417 --> 00:42:30.125
Didn't I greet you sweetly?

569
00:42:30.458 --> 00:42:32.042
Sure you did, Rayyan.

570
00:42:32.208 --> 00:42:33.625
I even smiled.

571
00:42:34.083 --> 00:42:37.542
- No, you didn't.
- What's his problem?

572
00:42:37.625 --> 00:42:38.875
Rayyan!

573
00:42:39.750 --> 00:42:40.875
Hello!

574
00:42:42.500 --> 00:42:43.875
Why don't you greet me back?

575
00:42:43.958 --> 00:42:46.750
- Rayyan…
- Hello!

576
00:42:47.000 --> 00:42:49.625
- Rayyan!
- Why are you so arrogant?

577
00:42:49.708 --> 00:42:51.125
Rayyan! Hey!

578
00:42:53.500 --> 00:42:56.167
Ten lashes! Take him away.

579
00:42:57.042 --> 00:42:58.250
Ten lashes!

580
00:42:59.417 --> 00:43:01.542
Sir! Those are not the rules, sir.

581
00:43:08.708 --> 00:43:09.708
Wait.

582
00:43:35.417 --> 00:43:38.250
Someone decided to wag his tongue.

583
00:43:39.042 --> 00:43:42.042
Please tell me. What are the rules?

584
00:43:44.083 --> 00:43:48.417
Sir, if three verbal warnings
have no effect

585
00:43:48.583 --> 00:43:51.458
then lashing can be prescribed
as a corrective measure.

586
00:43:52.375 --> 00:43:54.792
But first, three verbal warnings.

587
00:43:54.875 --> 00:43:56.458
That's what the book says, sir.

588
00:43:57.083 --> 00:43:59.250
You read your rule book?

589
00:43:59.875 --> 00:44:01.958
Makes me very happy, you know.

590
00:44:03.708 --> 00:44:05.292
Good for you!

591
00:44:05.958 --> 00:44:07.375
Let him go.

592
00:44:10.417 --> 00:44:13.333
- Carry on, carry on!
- Come on, guys.

593
00:44:14.458 --> 00:44:15.917
Let's play.

594
00:44:22.542 --> 00:44:23.833
Bro…

595
00:44:25.000 --> 00:44:28.042
I'm sorry. I owe you one.

596
00:44:41.667 --> 00:44:44.375
Ying Zhu has lots of electric problem.

597
00:44:44.667 --> 00:44:47.292
The electricity goes out often.

598
00:44:47.417 --> 00:44:50.458
God knows! But Hanshi Dao
always has electricity.

599
00:44:50.583 --> 00:44:52.417
There is always light.

600
00:44:52.708 --> 00:44:57.500
I need a house close to prison,
and I need a house which is cheap.

601
00:44:57.708 --> 00:45:01.000
- So…
- Long live revolution!

602
00:45:01.083 --> 00:45:04.917
- What did he write?
- It's written <i>"Geming Wansui"</i>!

603
00:45:05.000 --> 00:45:09.167
- Means?
- It means, long live revolution.

604
00:45:11.750 --> 00:45:16.542
This house is so cheap
because someone who lived here before

605
00:45:16.667 --> 00:45:18.667
took his own life.

606
00:45:19.250 --> 00:45:20.417
It's okay.

607
00:45:21.375 --> 00:45:23.542
I'm used to living in such houses.

608
00:45:25.000 --> 00:45:26.458
I'll be fine.

609
00:45:28.250 --> 00:45:32.208
<i>I appealed and got your sentence delayed
by four months.</i>

610
00:45:33.917 --> 00:45:36.083
<i>I'm meeting some top lawyers.</i>

611
00:45:36.625 --> 00:45:38.833
<i>We will continue
to prolong the case for some time.</i>

612
00:45:39.542 --> 00:45:42.625
<i>Don't worry, everything is under control.</i>

613
00:45:43.208 --> 00:45:46.375
<i>What are you saying, Sis?
Nothing is under control.</i>

614
00:45:51.667 --> 00:45:53.917
<i>I was talking to some inmates.</i>

615
00:45:54.708 --> 00:45:55.958
<i>They were saying</i>

616
00:45:56.458 --> 00:46:00.583
<i>you can keep delaying the execution,
but no one gets out of here alive.</i>

617
00:46:05.458 --> 00:46:07.333
<i>Sis, do you know
what kind of people they are?</i>

618
00:46:07.417 --> 00:46:10.750
<i>I'm on death row, yet they make me
clean the electric chair.</i>

619
00:46:11.625 --> 00:46:14.625
<i>They say it's the quickest
and least painful method of execution.</i>

620
00:46:17.375 --> 00:46:19.333
<i>Sis, they pardon no one.</i>

621
00:46:35.208 --> 00:46:38.750
<i>O heart!</i>

622
00:46:41.208 --> 00:46:43.875
<i>Every speck of it</i>

623
00:47:06.167 --> 00:47:08.292
Are they protesting?

624
00:47:08.542 --> 00:47:11.083
- Custom.
- What?

625
00:47:11.583 --> 00:47:12.625
Tradition.

626
00:47:13.750 --> 00:47:15.708
Some seek blessings.

627
00:47:15.833 --> 00:47:19.625
Some want to be pardoned.
Others offer hope

628
00:47:20.292 --> 00:47:22.333
so no prisoner stops hoping.

629
00:47:22.917 --> 00:47:25.708
Seems like your lawyers were useless, too.

630
00:47:26.667 --> 00:47:28.792
They're leaving him to die,

631
00:47:28.917 --> 00:47:31.208
while the authorities ask us
to light a lamp of hope.

632
00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:38.500
There's no choice. How much can one drink
sitting alone at home?

633
00:47:39.417 --> 00:47:42.250
- Shekhar Bhatia.
- Satya.

634
00:47:43.292 --> 00:47:44.667
Come, it's our turn.

635
00:47:47.667 --> 00:47:49.292
Who is inside?

636
00:47:50.500 --> 00:47:53.083
My son. What about you?

637
00:47:54.125 --> 00:47:55.125
My brother.

638
00:47:56.625 --> 00:47:59.333
Join us for the counseling session.

639
00:48:00.667 --> 00:48:02.167
Come, my dear…

640
00:48:03.833 --> 00:48:07.458
Okay. Satya, please come.

641
00:48:07.792 --> 00:48:09.167
Maximum 30 minutes.

642
00:48:09.750 --> 00:48:12.292
If nothing else,
enjoy the free tea and biscuits.

643
00:48:14.917 --> 00:48:19.792
Hope doesn't mean manifesting
the best possible outcome,

644
00:48:19.917 --> 00:48:25.333
but simply acknowledging
that hope itself is a living activity.

645
00:48:25.417 --> 00:48:30.958
Tonight we'll be talking about <i>Chi Ku</i>.

646
00:48:31.458 --> 00:48:35.042
Exploring the idea
that we can take on board our pain

647
00:48:35.167 --> 00:48:38.958
and suffering without complaining.
Behind me…

648
00:48:39.542 --> 00:48:41.333
Will he complain if I punch him?

649
00:48:43.833 --> 00:48:46.333
No one is forcing you to stay.
Leave if you want.

650
00:48:46.417 --> 00:48:48.125
Don't ruin it for others.

651
00:48:50.000 --> 00:48:51.708
I need to go to the washroom.

652
00:48:52.250 --> 00:48:53.958
I need to use the washroom.

653
00:48:54.208 --> 00:48:56.958
- I'll take her. It's okay.
- Okay.

654
00:48:57.792 --> 00:48:59.167
The seven stages…

655
00:48:59.292 --> 00:49:02.417
Denial, shock, depression,

656
00:49:02.958 --> 00:49:06.958
testing, anger, bargaining, and finally…

657
00:49:07.875 --> 00:49:09.167
acceptance.

658
00:49:09.583 --> 00:49:11.208
I'll be checking in with all of you.

659
00:49:11.292 --> 00:49:13.583
I can't do this.
It was very, very nice meeting you.

660
00:49:13.667 --> 00:49:15.833
You have my number. I'm leaving.

661
00:49:15.917 --> 00:49:18.125
- Stay a bit longer.
- I'm going...

662
00:49:18.292 --> 00:49:20.833
- Just a while…
- Sorry, is there a problem?

663
00:49:21.875 --> 00:49:23.333
Keep your <i>Chi Ku</i> to yourself.

664
00:49:23.417 --> 00:49:25.250
- I must go.
- Sorry, I don't understand.

665
00:49:25.333 --> 00:49:27.917
I don't want to accept what you're saying.

666
00:49:28.000 --> 00:49:28.833
Calm down.

667
00:49:28.917 --> 00:49:31.250
Come on, Mr. Bhatia.
I'm running out of time.

668
00:49:31.333 --> 00:49:34.083
My brother is about to be executed,
and he's talking about <i>Chi Ku</i>.

669
00:49:34.167 --> 00:49:35.958
You say, "calm down". He says, "accept".

670
00:49:36.042 --> 00:49:39.083
Accept? I'd rather bomb the jail
than accept.

671
00:49:39.208 --> 00:49:41.625
Did you say something about a bomb?

672
00:49:43.792 --> 00:49:44.958
Yeah, I did.

673
00:49:46.625 --> 00:49:51.000
This whole program
is designed for moments just like this.

674
00:49:51.500 --> 00:49:54.708
- There's this darkness…
- Does this make sense?

675
00:49:54.958 --> 00:49:57.042
- It's overwhelming you.
- Hey!

676
00:49:57.125 --> 00:50:00.583
Wrap this shit up! We've got a match!

677
00:50:00.917 --> 00:50:02.250
We better go.

678
00:50:02.375 --> 00:50:04.958
- It's Saturday. You talk too much.
- Let's go.

679
00:50:05.500 --> 00:50:06.333
Out!

680
00:50:06.417 --> 00:50:08.833
No. We're not going through
this again, please.

681
00:50:08.917 --> 00:50:10.708
Go! Get out!

682
00:50:11.083 --> 00:50:12.417
Okay.

683
00:50:12.500 --> 00:50:15.625
Go back to your druggies and murderers.
Leave!

684
00:50:15.708 --> 00:50:19.292
They deserve to die already!
Hang, hang like that!

685
00:50:21.000 --> 00:50:22.208
Go now.

686
00:50:23.208 --> 00:50:26.375
Don't play the hero, just save your skin.

687
00:50:27.458 --> 00:50:29.333
No, it's time to play the hero.

688
00:50:32.292 --> 00:50:34.125
Don't you understand English?

689
00:50:39.500 --> 00:50:40.500
Can I help you?

690
00:50:48.833 --> 00:50:49.833
Leave!

691
00:50:53.250 --> 00:50:54.542
Shall we go?

692
00:51:00.750 --> 00:51:03.208
You won't like
what's going to happen next.

693
00:51:04.583 --> 00:51:07.333
You should've left already
when I told you to.

694
00:51:08.250 --> 00:51:09.500
Pretty girl!

695
00:51:13.792 --> 00:51:15.250
He was in my face.

696
00:51:15.583 --> 00:51:17.542
Get her!

697
00:51:19.708 --> 00:51:21.375
I'm a tiger!

698
00:51:23.125 --> 00:51:25.083
Stop! It's enough. Enough.

699
00:51:26.125 --> 00:51:27.167
Why do you have a gun?

700
00:51:27.250 --> 00:51:29.667
- No! It's empty! No bullets.
- Call the police.

701
00:51:29.750 --> 00:51:32.500
No. No need of police! It's empty, safe.

702
00:51:32.750 --> 00:51:34.542
Everything is under control.

703
00:51:35.667 --> 00:51:37.208
No bullets.

704
00:51:40.500 --> 00:51:41.542
Are you okay, Counselor?

705
00:51:44.458 --> 00:51:47.167
You're a real thug.

706
00:51:47.958 --> 00:51:49.417
I used to be one, but I've retired.

707
00:51:50.083 --> 00:51:53.625
Had I met you 20 years ago,
I would've brought you into my gang.

708
00:51:54.833 --> 00:51:58.833
- Get your gun.
- Oh, yes. Sir, my gun.

709
00:51:59.917 --> 00:52:02.417
- You have a license?
- Of course! It's legal.

710
00:52:03.500 --> 00:52:06.875
Thank you. So, we're meeting at the bar.

711
00:52:07.375 --> 00:52:09.375
We will continue with the therapy.

712
00:52:09.500 --> 00:52:11.833
Drinks and food on me, sir. Relax.

713
00:52:11.917 --> 00:52:13.792
Everybody is invited! Come.

714
00:52:14.417 --> 00:52:17.375
- Is everyone okay?
- You're too much!

715
00:52:26.417 --> 00:52:28.208
Tony is the best.

716
00:52:29.625 --> 00:52:31.833
He was in the wrong place
at the wrong time.

717
00:52:32.500 --> 00:52:34.750
This is payback!

718
00:52:35.917 --> 00:52:37.417
It's unfair.

719
00:52:38.000 --> 00:52:42.208
Innocents always pay the price
for the crimes of others. It's nonsense!

720
00:52:44.042 --> 00:52:45.750
My poor son has epilepsy.

721
00:52:48.542 --> 00:52:50.417
How did your brother land in jail?

722
00:52:51.708 --> 00:52:53.292
My brother?

723
00:52:58.208 --> 00:53:00.583
He got taken for granted, Mr. Bhatia.

724
00:53:03.250 --> 00:53:05.208
Use and throw.

725
00:53:06.417 --> 00:53:10.625
How come?
What about your family? Your parents?

726
00:53:16.125 --> 00:53:17.375
God took my mother's life.

727
00:53:19.125 --> 00:53:20.625
And my father took his own life.

728
00:53:24.083 --> 00:53:27.792
Some relatives took care of me
and my brother

729
00:53:29.875 --> 00:53:32.125
but made us pay a hefty price.

730
00:53:34.542 --> 00:53:36.417
Let it go, Mr. Bhatia.

731
00:53:37.000 --> 00:53:42.042
It's a long story and my brother
has very little time left.

732
00:53:42.708 --> 00:53:44.167
Very little time.

733
00:53:44.375 --> 00:53:47.333
Let's blow up the damn prison!

734
00:53:49.625 --> 00:53:52.625
It was you who mentioned a bomb.

735
00:53:52.708 --> 00:53:57.000
So let's make a bomb
and set it off. Seriously.

736
00:53:57.083 --> 00:53:58.500
So you're serious?

737
00:53:59.000 --> 00:54:00.292
Okay.

738
00:54:01.708 --> 00:54:03.208
Jailbreak?

739
00:54:05.208 --> 00:54:07.583
Let's get the kids out.

740
00:54:10.000 --> 00:54:13.042
These children can't die in there, Satya.

741
00:54:20.875 --> 00:54:22.875
- Done.
- Done?

742
00:54:23.458 --> 00:54:24.458
Done.

743
00:54:25.833 --> 00:54:27.208
Done.

744
00:54:29.208 --> 00:54:31.333
Done.

745
00:54:31.833 --> 00:54:34.792
You have no idea
about the nonsense you talk.

746
00:54:36.125 --> 00:54:37.167
And you do?

747
00:54:38.375 --> 00:54:39.375
Yes.

748
00:54:40.083 --> 00:54:43.042
Actually, I do, I bloody well do!

749
00:54:43.625 --> 00:54:44.792
Tell me.

750
00:54:44.875 --> 00:54:47.292
The jail you're talking about…

751
00:54:49.667 --> 00:54:53.250
I've had many men imprisoned there
when I was in the police force.

752
00:54:53.333 --> 00:54:56.292
Oh, Mr. Muthu!

753
00:54:57.292 --> 00:55:00.958
Buddy, don't arrest me.
I'm a retired gangster.

754
00:55:01.042 --> 00:55:03.167
And I have a gun license.

755
00:55:03.750 --> 00:55:07.167
I quit the force.
I'm no longer a cop, Bhatia.

756
00:55:07.250 --> 00:55:10.583
Great! I'm retired, you're retired,

757
00:55:11.042 --> 00:55:12.875
and we have a new job now.

758
00:55:13.042 --> 00:55:17.750
Do you have a blueprint of the prison?

759
00:55:23.333 --> 00:55:26.792
That jail is impenetrable.

760
00:55:28.292 --> 00:55:29.292
So help us.

761
00:55:30.958 --> 00:55:32.042
Right?

762
00:55:32.292 --> 00:55:35.000
Will you let the person you love
die in there?

763
00:55:40.000 --> 00:55:42.750
Go home and sleep, Bhatia.
Don't play the tiger.

764
00:55:45.292 --> 00:55:46.542
You too, Satya.

765
00:55:56.125 --> 00:55:57.167
What's his story?

766
00:55:58.667 --> 00:55:59.667
Let's find out.

767
00:56:00.625 --> 00:56:04.042
Haven't you heard
that too many cooks spoil the broth?

768
00:56:05.000 --> 00:56:08.583
<i>Sharpen your knives</i>

769
00:56:09.333 --> 00:56:13.333
<i>I make a knife so sharp
It turns into a sword</i>

770
00:56:13.625 --> 00:56:17.917
<i>Try it once! You won't regret it</i>

771
00:56:18.167 --> 00:56:21.875
<i>Here, life is on a knife-edge</i>

772
00:56:22.542 --> 00:56:25.917
<i>So sharpen your knives…</i>

773
00:56:26.625 --> 00:56:30.000
Okay. So tell me.

774
00:56:30.917 --> 00:56:35.750
Mr. Bhatia, you kept saying "done"
in the bar and raised your glass.

775
00:56:36.333 --> 00:56:37.708
You did, too.

776
00:56:37.792 --> 00:56:42.792
- Because I trusted your experience.
- I'm retired. I carry an empty gun.

777
00:56:46.458 --> 00:56:48.583
Turn off your playlist, please!

778
00:56:54.042 --> 00:56:56.250
We won't make it without an insider.

779
00:56:56.708 --> 00:57:01.208
We can plan all we want,
but it will eventually lead to a dead end.

780
00:57:05.375 --> 00:57:07.958
There's no time for a hit-and-miss plan.

781
00:57:10.125 --> 00:57:12.708
We need to find out Muthu's full story.

782
00:57:13.083 --> 00:57:14.083
Agree?

783
00:57:14.875 --> 00:57:16.125
Absolutely.

784
00:57:18.542 --> 00:57:22.042
<i>My boys have informed me
that Muthu was born in India.</i>

785
00:57:22.833 --> 00:57:26.625
<i>He came to Hanshi Dao
when he was a teenager.</i>

786
00:57:27.667 --> 00:57:31.458
<i>He did his military service here
and got his citizenship.</i>

787
00:57:31.583 --> 00:57:33.292
<i>Then he joined the police.</i>

788
00:57:33.625 --> 00:57:36.167
<i>He had an Indian boy thrown into jail</i>

789
00:57:36.750 --> 00:57:39.292
<i>and later discovered the boy was innocent.</i>

790
00:57:40.125 --> 00:57:44.250
<i>He tried to save him,
but the kid got the death penalty.</i>

791
00:57:45.917 --> 00:57:49.667
<i>Muthu quit his job so he could try
to get the kid released.</i>

792
00:57:50.167 --> 00:57:52.917
<i>Well, he's a good guy.</i>

793
00:57:53.292 --> 00:57:56.333
Hello, Muthu.
No need to pay for the locker.

794
00:57:56.500 --> 00:57:57.708
It's okay, I'll pay for it.

795
00:57:57.792 --> 00:58:00.958
It's okay, no problem!
I'll take care of it. It's okay.

796
00:58:01.042 --> 00:58:02.208
Okay, thank you.

797
00:58:02.292 --> 00:58:07.167
Chandan, the appeal hearing is close.

798
00:58:08.083 --> 00:58:10.833
I won't let anything wrong happen.

799
00:58:11.167 --> 00:58:13.083
<i>It's too late for that.</i>

800
00:58:13.792 --> 00:58:15.042
<i>It's too late.</i>

801
00:58:16.750 --> 00:58:19.042
<i>This appeal will also get rejected</i>

802
00:58:19.208 --> 00:58:22.083
<i>and you will come to apologize again.
Right?</i>

803
00:58:23.375 --> 00:58:25.500
They cannot reject it, Chandan.

804
00:58:25.833 --> 00:58:29.625
You'll be fine. I'm trying my best.

805
00:58:30.458 --> 00:58:33.250
Trust me, Chandan. Please.

806
00:58:34.792 --> 00:58:36.875
You shouldn't have quit the force, Muthu.

807
00:58:36.958 --> 00:58:39.583
We all make mistakes. It's okay.

808
00:58:44.875 --> 00:58:46.250
Hey, Muthu!

809
00:58:49.542 --> 00:58:51.583
Chandan is not your son or brother.

810
00:58:51.667 --> 00:58:53.583
Do you care if he lives or dies?

811
00:58:53.667 --> 00:58:56.708
If you do care,
should you leave him to die?

812
00:58:56.833 --> 00:58:59.250
I have appealed.

813
00:58:59.667 --> 00:59:02.083
And I believe it will go through.
There is a system...

814
00:59:02.167 --> 00:59:03.958
Like hell, Muthu!

815
00:59:04.042 --> 00:59:05.917
I'll help them escape.

816
00:59:06.333 --> 00:59:09.833
I'll help Tony, Ankur and Chandan.
Do whatever you want to do.

817
00:59:09.917 --> 00:59:11.917
- Go.
- No, do what you have to do.

818
00:59:12.167 --> 00:59:14.292
Muthu, listen to me. Listen.

819
00:59:15.875 --> 00:59:17.292
Please help us.

820
00:59:17.667 --> 00:59:20.167
Muthu, we can't make it without you.

821
00:59:22.667 --> 00:59:24.292
They're going to die.

822
00:59:24.708 --> 00:59:27.083
This is the only way.

823
00:59:27.375 --> 00:59:29.792
This is not the only way, Satya.

824
00:59:30.042 --> 00:59:33.292
Go to court. If your brother is innocent,

825
00:59:33.417 --> 00:59:36.250
the law of my country will not fail you.

826
00:59:39.458 --> 00:59:41.833
What law? What country?

827
00:59:42.875 --> 00:59:46.167
People are fined if they laugh,
cry or breathe.

828
00:59:46.500 --> 00:59:50.083
The fines are used to make
everything perfect on the outside.

829
00:59:50.292 --> 00:59:55.167
If foreigners do anything wrong,
they're dead and buried.

830
00:59:55.292 --> 00:59:57.083
Isn't this how it works?

831
00:59:57.333 --> 01:00:01.417
Should I give you a list of things
happening in your country? Should I?

832
01:00:01.542 --> 01:00:03.167
Don't lecture me about our system.

833
01:00:03.250 --> 01:00:05.667
- Stop this nonsense, Satya.
- Or what?

834
01:00:05.792 --> 01:00:09.250
- I'll report you to the authorities now.
- Okay then, I'll just kill you.

835
01:00:13.375 --> 01:00:14.708
Want to fight?

836
01:00:15.917 --> 01:00:20.333
I'm not a street thug,
I'm a trained officer, Satya.

837
01:00:22.708 --> 01:00:24.375
I know karate.

838
01:00:25.542 --> 01:00:27.917
I have a yellow belt. Ting! Ting!

839
01:00:35.000 --> 01:00:37.917
Go ahead. I won't judge you if you hit me.

840
01:00:39.125 --> 01:00:40.125
Go away.

841
01:00:46.000 --> 01:00:49.417
Let's settle it.
If I win, you're in my team.

842
01:01:09.875 --> 01:01:11.875
Stay down.

843
01:01:43.917 --> 01:01:45.750
Oh, shit! Muthu?

844
01:01:46.792 --> 01:01:48.542
Oh, shit! Muthu!

845
01:01:49.792 --> 01:01:51.792
Oh, shit! Okay…

846
01:01:52.083 --> 01:01:53.667
Muthu!

847
01:01:56.000 --> 01:01:57.083
Shit.

848
01:01:57.458 --> 01:01:58.458
Muthu!

849
01:02:13.375 --> 01:02:15.958
Don't feel bad
that you lost to a yellow belt.

850
01:02:16.417 --> 01:02:18.542
They banned me from the competition,

851
01:02:19.333 --> 01:02:20.693
otherwise I would be a black belt.

852
01:02:26.125 --> 01:02:27.750
It wasn't their fault.

853
01:02:29.875 --> 01:02:32.208
They play by the rules…

854
01:02:34.083 --> 01:02:35.125
I don't.

855
01:02:46.583 --> 01:02:47.833
What do you say, Muthu?

856
01:02:51.250 --> 01:02:53.750
Tough. Satya is tough!

857
01:02:54.958 --> 01:02:56.083
I'm sorry.

858
01:02:56.667 --> 01:02:57.792
Don't be.

859
01:02:58.042 --> 01:02:59.042
I'm in.

860
01:03:48.458 --> 01:03:51.000
Our escape route is in this kitchen.

861
01:03:51.083 --> 01:03:53.667
We'll set it on fire, seal it from inside.

862
01:03:53.750 --> 01:03:55.375
Response time has to be fast.

863
01:03:55.458 --> 01:03:58.667
We start after dinner,
during cleaning time.

864
01:04:10.083 --> 01:04:13.417
Only two police officers inside,
post dinner lethargy…

865
01:04:13.542 --> 01:04:16.667
- Best time to attack.
- We will carry knives.

866
01:04:16.750 --> 01:04:18.625
- A cleaver.
- What?

867
01:04:21.458 --> 01:04:22.333
A cleaver?

868
01:04:22.417 --> 01:04:26.583
The cops will shoot the kids,
not bless them.

869
01:04:27.833 --> 01:04:31.000
I mean, if you want to feel good,
I can tell you to feel good.

870
01:04:36.542 --> 01:04:39.375
Okay, moving on. The boys are in control.

871
01:04:40.042 --> 01:04:43.250
Hopefully our luck will turn around
at this point.

872
01:04:43.458 --> 01:04:44.458
Yeah.

873
01:04:44.500 --> 01:04:49.292
Not everyone knows where the old block
blends into the new block.

874
01:04:49.583 --> 01:04:51.792
This information is gold.

875
01:04:52.417 --> 01:04:54.208
Which way does it go?

876
01:04:54.292 --> 01:04:57.708
It starts from here,
goes this way and comes out here.

877
01:05:05.583 --> 01:05:07.750
Muthu, you're a genius!

878
01:05:08.333 --> 01:05:09.333
Simple.

879
01:05:09.458 --> 01:05:13.042
It's so simple that no one
has ever thought of it before. Great!

880
01:05:13.125 --> 01:05:16.667
God is within us, yet we seek Him
elsewhere. So simple!

881
01:05:16.750 --> 01:05:19.000
Hold on, there's a problem.

882
01:05:19.500 --> 01:05:23.958
The kitchen sewer runs to Dragon Alley
and that's in the old block.

883
01:05:24.667 --> 01:05:30.042
In the new block, a 21 feet
concrete slab will come in our way.

884
01:05:31.458 --> 01:05:33.667
We have to build a tunnel
in order to get the boys out.

885
01:05:46.292 --> 01:05:49.583
Satya,
this brings back childhood memories.

886
01:05:50.917 --> 01:05:53.625
Studying for two hours before the exams,

887
01:05:55.125 --> 01:05:57.542
and yet always passing.

888
01:05:59.500 --> 01:06:01.458
<i>Once they're in the old sewers,</i>

889
01:06:01.542 --> 01:06:06.875
<i>they'll head to Dragon Alley,
then straight to the jetty.</i>

890
01:06:08.500 --> 01:06:10.417
<i>The Johor Strait waters
are split into three</i>

891
01:06:10.500 --> 01:06:13.000
<i>between Malaysia, Singapore,
and Hanshi Dao.</i>

892
01:06:13.083 --> 01:06:16.667
Once we've crossed the border,
we'll be in Malaysian waters

893
01:06:16.833 --> 01:06:18.792
where the Hanshi Dao police cannot enter.

894
01:06:18.875 --> 01:06:20.875
There's no extradition treaty either.

895
01:06:20.958 --> 01:06:22.750
Once we escape the Hanshi Dao cops,

896
01:06:22.833 --> 01:06:25.417
the Malaysian coast guard
will be after us.

897
01:06:25.792 --> 01:06:28.792
- That means trouble.
- I have a friend in the Malaysian Navy.

898
01:06:28.875 --> 01:06:31.250
We went to college together in Singapore.

899
01:06:31.333 --> 01:06:35.167
But I cannot expect free favors,
and I will tell him the truth.

900
01:06:35.292 --> 01:06:39.333
Wow! A friend you have to pay,
and be honest with?

901
01:06:39.458 --> 01:06:42.458
- Muthu, you call him a friend?
- He's an honest officer.

902
01:06:42.542 --> 01:06:44.625
I have to give him
a good reason to help us.

903
01:06:44.708 --> 01:06:47.083
I'll explain the whole situation to him,

904
01:06:47.208 --> 01:06:50.542
and tell him that we'll be posing
as doctors without borders.

905
01:06:50.625 --> 01:06:53.208
Doctors without borders?

906
01:06:54.750 --> 01:06:58.750
Okay, Google.
Search "Doctors Without Borders".

907
01:07:00.625 --> 01:07:03.125
International medical…

908
01:07:03.917 --> 01:07:07.292
Aren't we relying too much
on your friend and this technicality?

909
01:07:08.042 --> 01:07:11.750
<i>Yes, but this is the only way.</i>

910
01:07:13.125 --> 01:07:14.250
<i>Okay, I trust you.</i>

911
01:07:17.792 --> 01:07:20.292
- Pass me the map.
- Muthu, listen.

912
01:07:20.458 --> 01:07:23.958
Can you simplify this?

913
01:07:25.083 --> 01:07:27.000
We're not making a movie.

914
01:07:27.750 --> 01:07:29.250
This is complicated.

915
01:07:31.000 --> 01:07:32.792
<i>- Let's recap again.
- Okay.</i>

916
01:07:32.875 --> 01:07:35.500
<i>First, we must get the boys
assigned to kitchen duty.</i>

917
01:07:35.583 --> 01:07:37.559
<i>Then Bhatia will explain
the plan to his son, Tony.</i>

918
01:07:37.583 --> 01:07:40.417
<i>- Not too soon, not too late.
- Correct.</i>

919
01:07:50.417 --> 01:07:51.625
Do I look sad?

920
01:07:52.583 --> 01:07:53.750
Not at all!

921
01:07:57.000 --> 01:07:58.333
<i>You're getting out!</i>

922
01:07:59.750 --> 01:08:01.292
<i>Start the countdown.</i>

923
01:08:01.917 --> 01:08:03.292
<i>Done!</i>

924
01:08:04.333 --> 01:08:06.917
<i>Don't worry about me.
Take care of yourself.</i>

925
01:08:07.250 --> 01:08:08.333
<i>Eat on time.</i>

926
01:08:12.833 --> 01:08:14.750
<i>Eat on time?</i>

927
01:08:16.375 --> 01:08:18.135
<i>What happened
to "stay hungry, stay foolish"?</i>

928
01:08:20.292 --> 01:08:22.583
<i>You were never foolish, Sis.</i>

929
01:08:23.750 --> 01:08:24.958
<i>You were never foolish.</i>

930
01:08:29.375 --> 01:08:30.917
<i>You're hiding something.</i>

931
01:08:35.042 --> 01:08:37.125
<i>Is anyone giving you a hard time?</i>

932
01:08:59.208 --> 01:09:04.042
Why have you made this hook?
An extra hook? May I ask?

933
01:09:05.083 --> 01:09:06.875
Sir, this is for wet clothes.

934
01:09:07.167 --> 01:09:08.934
It's just to keep them separate
from dry clothes.

935
01:09:08.958 --> 01:09:12.208
But it's an extra hook. Extra!

936
01:09:13.792 --> 01:09:14.958
You know the rules!

937
01:09:15.042 --> 01:09:19.167
Any modification or modifications
made to your cell

938
01:09:19.250 --> 01:09:23.000
beyond what has been ideally
and wisely provided by the State

939
01:09:23.083 --> 01:09:26.750
for your rehabilitation
will be considered a violation.

940
01:09:30.625 --> 01:09:32.500
And the punishment for this violation

941
01:09:33.375 --> 01:09:36.500
is ten lashes and five salty lashes.

942
01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:39.167
Rules are rules, my friend.

943
01:09:40.333 --> 01:09:41.625
Bring him in!

944
01:09:42.750 --> 01:09:46.500
In your case,
I've taken an executive decision.

945
01:09:47.167 --> 01:09:51.500
I've taken the help of a volunteer
who will execute these lashes.

946
01:09:52.667 --> 01:09:57.833
Each lash will be hit with the same power
and same intensity.

947
01:09:58.875 --> 01:10:00.750
I will be the judge.

948
01:10:01.958 --> 01:10:06.167
If the volunteer does not fulfill
his responsibility

949
01:10:06.250 --> 01:10:08.000
to the best of his ability,

950
01:10:08.708 --> 01:10:12.250
then the volunteer
will also be liable to punishment.

951
01:10:12.583 --> 01:10:14.250
Same punishment.

952
01:10:14.917 --> 01:10:18.375
Ten lashes and five salted lashes.

953
01:10:20.542 --> 01:10:22.792
You understand, Mr. Rayyan?

954
01:10:26.375 --> 01:10:31.792
Each lash should have
the same power, and same intensity.

955
01:10:32.708 --> 01:10:34.333
Begin!

956
01:11:22.292 --> 01:11:23.292
Good!

957
01:11:23.958 --> 01:11:25.208
Five to go.

958
01:11:25.875 --> 01:11:27.417
Give him the salted lash.

959
01:12:19.542 --> 01:12:22.208
Good. Good, Mr. Rayyan.

960
01:12:22.708 --> 01:12:24.083
Well done.

961
01:12:24.833 --> 01:12:26.250
Take him back to his cell.

962
01:12:45.125 --> 01:12:48.333
Stupid boy, bloody stupid!

963
01:13:09.375 --> 01:13:10.958
<i>Made any friends?</i>

964
01:13:13.167 --> 01:13:15.458
<i>This is a jail, Sis, not a summer camp.</i>

965
01:13:27.042 --> 01:13:29.000
If I had greeted you back the other day

966
01:13:31.500 --> 01:13:33.167
the matter would've ended there.

967
01:13:35.833 --> 01:13:39.417
Would I care if you had got punished?

968
01:13:42.875 --> 01:13:43.917
But no.

969
01:13:46.000 --> 01:13:48.833
Ankur Anand was hell-bent

970
01:13:48.958 --> 01:13:50.500
on explaining the rules to OIC Landa.

971
01:13:54.000 --> 01:13:55.042
There's a saying…

972
01:13:57.667 --> 01:13:59.000
"You hit…"

973
01:13:59.333 --> 01:14:03.167
You hit the bull's eye. Bull's eye!

974
01:14:04.292 --> 01:14:05.625
Ankur Anand.

975
01:14:07.208 --> 01:14:08.500
You will not die in here.

976
01:14:10.375 --> 01:14:11.667
You will go home.

977
01:14:13.542 --> 01:14:17.292
You will live your life as a free man.

978
01:14:19.333 --> 01:14:20.333
Free?

979
01:14:23.208 --> 01:14:24.208
Jailbreak?

980
01:14:32.958 --> 01:14:34.542
Is anyone looking out for you?

981
01:14:35.583 --> 01:14:39.250
- Only my sister.
- Don't tell her about this.

982
01:14:42.708 --> 01:14:46.375
I said to you that I owe you one.

983
01:14:53.667 --> 01:14:56.958
You know the old unused toilet
in the medical ward?

984
01:14:57.250 --> 01:14:59.667
The one everyone believes is haunted.

985
01:15:00.083 --> 01:15:01.542
That's our way out.

986
01:15:03.083 --> 01:15:04.083
Come here.

987
01:15:06.917 --> 01:15:10.333
<i>Chandan, Matthew and I
volunteer there a lot.</i>

988
01:15:10.542 --> 01:15:14.833
<i>And Tony, being epileptic,
is often admitted there.</i>

989
01:15:24.167 --> 01:15:26.792
<i>Whenever one of us is volunteering,</i>

990
01:15:27.292 --> 01:15:29.333
<i>we start digging after lights out.</i>

991
01:15:33.125 --> 01:15:34.833
Come on, good goal.

992
01:15:35.333 --> 01:15:39.292
I'll talk to the prison officer and get
you transferred to the infirmary, okay?

993
01:15:40.167 --> 01:15:43.750
<i>We started digging a tunnel two years ago.</i>

994
01:15:43.833 --> 01:15:46.167
<i>It's almost ready.</i>

995
01:15:46.333 --> 01:15:48.042
<i>Once we climb over the wall</i>

996
01:15:48.625 --> 01:15:52.000
<i>we'll be in the main sewers.</i>

997
01:15:53.917 --> 01:15:57.625
<i>Then it's the jetty, and off we fly!</i>

998
01:16:24.917 --> 01:16:26.125
<i>You're getting out!</i>

999
01:16:27.625 --> 01:16:29.208
<i>Start the countdown.</i>

1000
01:16:29.792 --> 01:16:31.208
<i>Done!</i>

1001
01:16:32.208 --> 01:16:34.708
<i>Don't worry about me.
Take care of yourself.</i>

1002
01:16:35.083 --> 01:16:36.208
<i>Eat on time.</i>

1003
01:16:40.583 --> 01:16:42.458
<i>Eat on time?</i>

1004
01:16:44.208 --> 01:16:46.750
What happened
to "stay hungry, stay foolish"?

1005
01:16:47.500 --> 01:16:48.875
<i>You were never foolish, Sis.</i>

1006
01:16:50.875 --> 01:16:52.167
<i>You were never foolish.</i>

1007
01:16:56.542 --> 01:16:57.792
<i>You're hiding something.</i>

1008
01:17:02.708 --> 01:17:04.292
<i>Is anyone giving you a hard time?</i>

1009
01:17:05.458 --> 01:17:10.250
<i>Who would dare to do that
when I have you for a sister?</i>

1010
01:17:12.542 --> 01:17:14.417
<i>One in a million.</i>

1011
01:17:15.833 --> 01:17:20.542
<i>Even if the stars disappear
Or the moon hides…</i>

1012
01:17:21.292 --> 01:17:24.125
<i>Oh, you're all grown up now.</i>

1013
01:17:26.667 --> 01:17:28.434
<i>If the death sentence
wasn't hanging over you,</i>

1014
01:17:28.458 --> 01:17:30.333
<i>I would ask you to stay here longer!</i>

1015
01:17:32.625 --> 01:17:36.833
<i>Whether something happens or not</i>

1016
01:17:37.083 --> 01:17:39.958
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

1017
01:17:47.625 --> 01:17:51.958
<i>If a terrible storm encircles you</i>

1018
01:17:52.167 --> 01:17:54.792
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

1019
01:18:01.542 --> 01:18:05.792
<i>Even if the stars disappear
Or the moon hides</i>

1020
01:18:06.000 --> 01:18:08.917
<i>I'll keep you close</i>

1021
01:19:25.083 --> 01:19:30.125
This is his last photograph taken by us.
This is tradition.

1022
01:19:30.583 --> 01:19:33.167
The same will happen with the four of you.

1023
01:19:37.000 --> 01:19:39.958
I must say, I was surprised.

1024
01:19:40.667 --> 01:19:42.375
Surprised that he never told you.

1025
01:19:42.958 --> 01:19:45.625
I thought you guys were very close.

1026
01:19:47.625 --> 01:19:49.333
You know he found out last week, right?

1027
01:20:12.667 --> 01:20:14.167
Just give them a minute.

1028
01:20:14.375 --> 01:20:18.042
Let them compose themselves,
then you take them back to their cells.

1029
01:20:18.125 --> 01:20:19.417
Carry on.

1030
01:20:22.167 --> 01:20:24.792
How could he leave without telling us?

1031
01:20:24.875 --> 01:20:27.000
He was worried about us.

1032
01:20:27.292 --> 01:20:31.292
He knew that if we found out

1033
01:20:32.500 --> 01:20:34.458
we would speed up our plan.

1034
01:20:43.875 --> 01:20:45.042
Fifteen days to go.

1035
01:20:46.417 --> 01:20:47.917
Start the countdown.

1036
01:20:56.542 --> 01:21:01.583
<i>After 15 days, there's Zhongyuan,
the Hungry Ghost Festival.</i>

1037
01:21:02.458 --> 01:21:06.000
<i>We believe the doors of Hell
open wide on this day</i>

1038
01:21:06.208 --> 01:21:10.708
<i>and the dead souls roam freely
in our world.</i>

1039
01:21:11.417 --> 01:21:14.583
Towards the end of the festival,
we say goodbye to everyone

1040
01:21:15.167 --> 01:21:18.750
and their leader, Tai Tse Wong,
Hell's policeman.

1041
01:21:20.167 --> 01:21:21.625
Does it attract big crowds?

1042
01:21:23.375 --> 01:21:26.208
Yes, and a lot of the force
will be off duty, too.

1043
01:21:26.292 --> 01:21:29.833
It's a local belief
that Hell's policeman will be watching.

1044
01:21:30.125 --> 01:21:32.667
So fewer crimes take place,
statistically speaking.

1045
01:21:32.750 --> 01:21:34.792
The Guardian of Hell!

1046
01:21:35.083 --> 01:21:37.583
Some of my boys
also wouldn't work on that day.

1047
01:21:37.667 --> 01:21:40.167
Both thieves and cops have the day off.

1048
01:21:40.792 --> 01:21:42.417
Do you believe in it?

1049
01:21:42.875 --> 01:21:44.333
What is clear, Satya,

1050
01:21:44.458 --> 01:21:47.042
is that it's the best time
to plan an escape.

1051
01:21:50.625 --> 01:21:53.167
Our wishes will surely be granted!

1052
01:22:08.042 --> 01:22:09.792
Sir.

1053
01:22:09.875 --> 01:22:11.542
Can I get your signature?

1054
01:22:16.667 --> 01:22:18.750
- New cooks?
- Yes, sir.

1055
01:22:19.792 --> 01:22:22.708
I hope they're good,
otherwise good luck to them.

1056
01:22:22.833 --> 01:22:24.042
Thank you, sir.

1057
01:22:26.042 --> 01:22:27.625
Listen up!

1058
01:22:28.625 --> 01:22:31.083
I'm assigning your duties.

1059
01:22:31.792 --> 01:22:32.917
Rayyan,

1060
01:22:33.292 --> 01:22:37.333
Nathan, William, infirmary duty.

1061
01:22:38.167 --> 01:22:41.750
John Woo, Wong Kar-wai, Kim Ki-duk,

1062
01:22:42.083 --> 01:22:45.458
Chandan, Tony, Ankur,

1063
01:22:45.750 --> 01:22:48.250
kitchen duty…

1064
01:22:48.458 --> 01:22:49.750
What's wrong?

1065
01:22:49.917 --> 01:22:51.833
You guys are on kitchen duty.

1066
01:22:52.208 --> 01:22:53.625
What!

1067
01:22:54.833 --> 01:22:57.667
We were supposed
to volunteer at the infirmary.

1068
01:22:59.500 --> 01:23:01.167
Is this your father's doing?

1069
01:23:01.333 --> 01:23:03.458
Are you crazy? He isn't capable of this.

1070
01:23:41.875 --> 01:23:44.833
Move! Keep moving.

1071
01:23:51.042 --> 01:23:53.750
The Sicilian Mafia used the sheep code.

1072
01:23:54.417 --> 01:23:57.708
This is the Punjabi version of it.

1073
01:23:58.917 --> 01:24:01.125
I was often in and out of jail.

1074
01:24:01.375 --> 01:24:05.458
I would message Tony
the location of the drugs in code language

1075
01:24:05.667 --> 01:24:07.833
<i>and he would pass on the information.</i>

1076
01:25:28.458 --> 01:25:30.792
Everything depends on this, Bhatia.

1077
01:25:31.125 --> 01:25:34.083
Will Tony crack the code?
He won't panic, will he?

1078
01:25:34.792 --> 01:25:37.917
<i>Don't go by his looks.
He is a gangster's son.</i>

1079
01:25:38.667 --> 01:25:41.542
<i>But can he explain it
to Ankur and Chandan on time?</i>

1080
01:25:41.625 --> 01:25:42.750
<i>Hundred percent!</i>

1081
01:25:44.000 --> 01:25:46.083
<i>He is a tiger.</i>

1082
01:26:10.417 --> 01:26:11.667
Easy!

1083
01:26:24.042 --> 01:26:25.375
Go, Tiger!

1084
01:26:57.625 --> 01:27:01.167
This meeting is canceled.

1085
01:27:01.917 --> 01:27:04.083
- What?
- This meeting is canceled.

1086
01:27:04.208 --> 01:27:05.625
No, no, no!

1087
01:27:05.750 --> 01:27:09.708
No, no, no! I have to meet my son.

1088
01:27:10.667 --> 01:27:12.542
- This meeting is canceled.
- I have to…

1089
01:27:12.625 --> 01:27:15.750
It's a mistake! See? My meeting…

1090
01:27:15.833 --> 01:27:17.375
- What is this?
- My boy…

1091
01:27:17.458 --> 01:27:19.042
- I have to…
- What is the problem?

1092
01:27:19.125 --> 01:27:20.625
I have to meet my son.

1093
01:27:20.750 --> 01:27:23.375
- No visit today.
- I have to meet my son.

1094
01:27:23.500 --> 01:27:26.042
- No visit today!
- I have to meet my son!

1095
01:27:26.125 --> 01:27:27.167
He is in the medical ward.

1096
01:27:28.083 --> 01:27:30.333
- No!
- Medical ward?

1097
01:27:31.583 --> 01:27:32.704
- Why the medical ward?
- No.

1098
01:27:32.750 --> 01:27:35.625
- No, no, no! He is okay.
- Let me go.

1099
01:27:35.708 --> 01:27:38.125
- I have to meet my son.
- No, no, no! He is okay.

1100
01:27:38.208 --> 01:27:40.417
I have to meet my son.

1101
01:27:40.542 --> 01:27:43.458
Go, go…

1102
01:27:52.375 --> 01:27:55.083
<i>So what if you aren't working
in the medical ward?</i>

1103
01:27:55.167 --> 01:27:57.500
<i>Go there as a patient.</i>

1104
01:28:06.042 --> 01:28:09.500
<i>Mix these cleaning pods in your food.</i>

1105
01:28:10.542 --> 01:28:13.000
<i>They'll have an effect in an hour.</i>

1106
01:28:13.458 --> 01:28:17.583
<i>You might feel like you're dying,
but don't get scared.</i>

1107
01:28:18.083 --> 01:28:21.167
<i>This is the only way to get into the ward.</i>

1108
01:28:21.292 --> 01:28:23.917
<i>See you boys
once you've puked your guts out!</i>

1109
01:28:24.500 --> 01:28:30.167
<i>The whole sky in a single bird</i>

1110
01:28:31.125 --> 01:28:36.417
<i>The whole ocean in a single fish</i>

1111
01:28:37.542 --> 01:28:43.208
<i>Like a firefly burning in my night</i>

1112
01:28:44.333 --> 01:28:49.875
<i>Your words blend into mine</i>

1113
01:28:51.833 --> 01:28:54.667
<i>O heart!</i>

1114
01:28:56.042 --> 01:28:58.375
<i>Every speck of it</i>

1115
01:28:58.458 --> 01:29:01.292
<i>O heart!</i>

1116
01:29:03.000 --> 01:29:07.542
<i>Searching for you in every story</i>

1117
01:29:07.958 --> 01:29:12.000
<i>A star shining on my destiny</i>

1118
01:29:12.083 --> 01:29:15.667
<i>O heart!</i>

1119
01:29:16.208 --> 01:29:18.708
<i>Every speck of it</i>

1120
01:29:25.250 --> 01:29:27.500
Okay. Thanks, man.

1121
01:29:28.500 --> 01:29:31.458
Food poisoning, vomiting and fever.

1122
01:29:32.333 --> 01:29:36.542
- Now they'll have to rest.
- We'll miss the Hungry Ghost Festival.

1123
01:29:36.667 --> 01:29:40.750
We've timed everything according to it.

1124
01:29:41.250 --> 01:29:43.417
What if there's a medical emergency?

1125
01:29:43.667 --> 01:29:46.625
Will they let me see Ankur
if I slash my wrists?

1126
01:29:46.708 --> 01:29:48.417
Satya, put that knife away.

1127
01:29:48.500 --> 01:29:50.958
No, I'm being practical.
Would they let me see Ankur

1128
01:29:51.042 --> 01:29:52.875
in a life and death situation?

1129
01:29:52.958 --> 01:29:55.792
I can at least explain
the plan to him that way.

1130
01:29:55.875 --> 01:29:58.750
Don't be crazy. Give me that knife.

1131
01:29:59.333 --> 01:30:02.250
Muthu, I'm not being dramatic. Okay?
Just tell me the rules.

1132
01:30:02.333 --> 01:30:04.250
Can an inmate meet a family member

1133
01:30:04.333 --> 01:30:06.750
in a life and death situation?
It's very simple.

1134
01:30:06.833 --> 01:30:09.750
Satya, this is a bad idea.

1135
01:30:10.417 --> 01:30:12.375
Please give me that knife. Please.

1136
01:30:12.458 --> 01:30:16.250
<i>O heart…</i>

1137
01:30:17.750 --> 01:30:20.750
We'll miss the Hungry Ghost Festival!

1138
01:30:21.167 --> 01:30:24.750
Our plans are timed according to it,
Muthu.

1139
01:30:26.750 --> 01:30:27.750
Satya.

1140
01:30:31.083 --> 01:30:32.750
We have no option.

1141
01:30:34.042 --> 01:30:35.167
This plan is aborted.

1142
01:30:48.667 --> 01:30:50.208
- Smoke?
- No.

1143
01:30:50.875 --> 01:30:52.208
Come on!

1144
01:30:54.583 --> 01:30:56.333
- Come on.
- Okay, let's go.

1145
01:31:44.875 --> 01:31:46.708
Chandan, get in.

1146
01:32:08.750 --> 01:32:11.292
Why are the same three names
on two different lists?

1147
01:32:11.375 --> 01:32:14.333
Nobody is checking, is it?
Is everyone on holiday?

1148
01:32:15.000 --> 01:32:17.333
And the same three people
are sick in the medical ward?

1149
01:32:17.417 --> 01:32:18.708
Is no one checking?

1150
01:32:46.375 --> 01:32:47.625
I love you.

1151
01:32:48.708 --> 01:32:49.792
I know.

1152
01:32:50.292 --> 01:32:51.708
Thank you.

1153
01:32:52.792 --> 01:32:54.208
Keep moving.

1154
01:33:08.292 --> 01:33:11.583
Escaped prisoners! Holiday over.

1155
01:33:33.875 --> 01:33:37.000
Hey, Rayyan! Why didn't you tell us?

1156
01:33:37.833 --> 01:33:40.667
Never reveal all your cards!

1157
01:33:42.375 --> 01:33:43.625
Come on.

1158
01:33:53.708 --> 01:33:55.125
Hold this.

1159
01:35:11.708 --> 01:35:12.958
What's in the letter?

1160
01:35:16.583 --> 01:35:17.625
Satya?

1161
01:35:18.583 --> 01:35:19.875
What's wrong, Satya?

1162
01:35:21.708 --> 01:35:24.792
Are you okay? What's in the letter?

1163
01:35:50.000 --> 01:35:54.333
These are their last photographs
taken by us.

1164
01:35:59.792 --> 01:36:01.625
Run!

1165
01:37:08.500 --> 01:37:10.292
I would like to take this moment

1166
01:37:10.667 --> 01:37:15.292
to extend the State's
and my condolences for your loss.

1167
01:37:22.500 --> 01:37:23.958
I'm sorry, Chandan.

1168
01:37:30.750 --> 01:37:34.083
Who would send anyone a photo like this?

1169
01:37:36.542 --> 01:37:39.833
This is his last photo, Satya.

1170
01:37:48.542 --> 01:37:50.333
It's not his last photo.

1171
01:37:52.542 --> 01:37:55.875
Satya, it's over.

1172
01:37:57.292 --> 01:37:58.625
Nothing can be done now.

1173
01:38:10.333 --> 01:38:12.500
How do they get their electricity?

1174
01:38:14.500 --> 01:38:15.958
From generators.

1175
01:38:16.833 --> 01:38:18.875
The island has diesel generators.

1176
01:38:21.125 --> 01:38:26.375
If they stop working,
there will be no power on the island

1177
01:38:27.917 --> 01:38:28.917
or in the prison.

1178
01:38:30.042 --> 01:38:32.083
The jail is electronic.

1179
01:38:32.708 --> 01:38:36.833
The locks and the security system,
nothing works without power.

1180
01:38:37.833 --> 01:38:39.333
They have backup generators

1181
01:38:40.292 --> 01:38:42.792
because Ying Zhu's power supply
is unstable.

1182
01:38:42.917 --> 01:38:45.208
Their generators are refueled every day.

1183
01:38:45.292 --> 01:38:47.333
The backup is solid.

1184
01:38:49.125 --> 01:38:52.750
Let's shut down their backups
and then the main generator.

1185
01:38:53.458 --> 01:38:55.167
What are you saying?

1186
01:38:55.792 --> 01:38:57.625
If you succeed by any chance,

1187
01:38:57.708 --> 01:39:01.333
the jail will be wide open
and all the prisoners could escape.

1188
01:39:01.417 --> 01:39:03.333
Six thousand of them!

1189
01:39:04.750 --> 01:39:08.792
That will include Ankur,
Chandan, and Tony, right?

1190
01:39:10.458 --> 01:39:12.083
- Are you being serious?
- Yes.

1191
01:39:13.000 --> 01:39:14.875
There's a difference

1192
01:39:15.125 --> 01:39:20.708
between saving three innocent lives
and letting 6,000 convicts escape.

1193
01:39:20.875 --> 01:39:23.792
Forget the authorities,
I won't let this happen.

1194
01:39:24.625 --> 01:39:29.542
Muthu, Ankur cannot die.

1195
01:39:31.833 --> 01:39:35.042
I wish to save Chandan
under any circumstances.

1196
01:39:35.292 --> 01:39:38.708
I'm ready to die to save him,
but not like this.

1197
01:39:39.292 --> 01:39:42.333
I can't let 6,000 criminals escape, Satya.

1198
01:39:42.958 --> 01:39:44.750
This is very wrong.

1199
01:39:48.542 --> 01:39:50.125
You're right, Muthu.

1200
01:39:51.417 --> 01:39:52.750
I'm wrong.

1201
01:39:55.292 --> 01:39:57.250
I never claimed to be ethical.

1202
01:39:59.708 --> 01:40:02.000
What I am is Ankur's sister.

1203
01:40:09.292 --> 01:40:10.500
Don't be a part of it,

1204
01:40:11.667 --> 01:40:13.542
but don't come in my way.

1205
01:40:43.833 --> 01:40:45.000
Satya…

1206
01:40:45.833 --> 01:40:48.292
Satya, let me tell you the story

1207
01:40:48.750 --> 01:40:52.583
of the scorpion and the frog.

1208
01:40:52.708 --> 01:40:54.625
Not that story again.

1209
01:40:54.750 --> 01:40:57.708
Satya, I don't have plans

1210
01:40:58.042 --> 01:41:00.000
but I do have stories.

1211
01:41:03.667 --> 01:41:05.333
- There was once a rat.
- Okay.

1212
01:41:05.458 --> 01:41:09.000
He fell into the water,
and he gasped for air for 15 minutes.

1213
01:41:09.083 --> 01:41:11.833
He was about to die when he found a stick.

1214
01:41:12.042 --> 01:41:13.792
- Wow!
- The rat held on to it

1215
01:41:14.417 --> 01:41:16.333
and could breathe.

1216
01:41:16.708 --> 01:41:20.583
He rested a while
and ate the leaves stuck on the stick.

1217
01:41:21.667 --> 01:41:23.625
Then the stick drifted away.

1218
01:41:25.000 --> 01:41:29.125
Guess how long the rat
managed to stay alive?

1219
01:41:31.667 --> 01:41:33.792
Ten minutes? 15 minutes? 20?

1220
01:41:34.042 --> 01:41:35.292
Guess again.

1221
01:41:35.500 --> 01:41:37.458
Half an hour, an hour?

1222
01:41:38.792 --> 01:41:39.792
Sixty hours!

1223
01:41:39.958 --> 01:41:42.125
That's amazing, Satya!

1224
01:41:42.958 --> 01:41:44.542
In round two,

1225
01:41:44.875 --> 01:41:48.458
the rat not only survived, but smashed it.

1226
01:41:49.083 --> 01:41:50.542
Totally smashed it!

1227
01:41:55.750 --> 01:41:57.375
Search it on Google.

1228
01:41:57.792 --> 01:41:59.458
"Hope experiment with rats."

1229
01:41:59.625 --> 01:42:01.500
I don't want Google wisdom.

1230
01:42:01.625 --> 01:42:04.500
Just tell me how to smash it.

1231
01:42:06.000 --> 01:42:09.792
My favourite method. Fire!

1232
01:42:11.125 --> 01:42:14.875
Fire? Petrol? We don't have
any money left, Satya.

1233
01:42:15.000 --> 01:42:16.500
Sell your jewellery!

1234
01:42:17.583 --> 01:42:18.875
<i>I got the fire</i>

1235
01:42:21.542 --> 01:42:23.542
<i>I got the fire</i>

1236
01:42:25.292 --> 01:42:27.250
<i>I got the fire</i>

1237
01:42:30.167 --> 01:42:32.042
Boys, I'm back!

1238
01:42:32.750 --> 01:42:34.625
Let's get back to work.

1239
01:42:34.708 --> 01:42:36.458
<i>Fan the flames</i>

1240
01:42:37.250 --> 01:42:38.542
<i>There's a fire in me</i>

1241
01:42:38.625 --> 01:42:40.125
<i>Fan the flames</i>

1242
01:42:40.250 --> 01:42:42.750
<i>Burn betrayal with justice</i>

1243
01:42:43.083 --> 01:42:46.042
<i>The fire will win! There's a fire in me</i>

1244
01:42:46.167 --> 01:42:49.167
<i>Cross all lines! Set the world aflame</i>

1245
01:42:51.125 --> 01:42:53.083
<i>I got the fire</i>

1246
01:42:55.000 --> 01:42:56.875
<i>I got the fire</i>

1247
01:42:58.875 --> 01:43:04.292
<i>I got the fire</i>

1248
